helps in increasing customer loyalty, brand awareness, etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Stay Ahead of Competition\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A professional website maintenance company always leverages cutting-edge tools to gather relevant data and update your website accordingly. It’s one of the top benefits of website maintenance. They gather data related to your customers’ behavior.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>With this data, these professionals get an idea about what works the best for your website in terms of what visitors prefer the most. And they focus on those items that work best and do necessary updates for your website accordingly.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>In this way, regular and constant updates of your business website are a better way to outrank competitors easily. Once your website ranks well in search engines, it not only improves the ranking of the website but also helps it stand out from the competition.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Acquire New Customers with Improved Retention\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Acquiring new customers constantly reflects that your business is progressive. Increasing customer retention, on the other hand, makes your business reliable and thus more customer-centric. An outdated website will not cater to your needs.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The major benefit of website maintenance is you find it quite easier to optimize the overall performance of your website. Professionals who are responsible for updating your website work with a thorough plan.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>They work with a clear mechanism to analyze the speed of your website and thus, enable you to avoid any kind of issues related to the performance of your website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Partnering with a reliable website maintenance service provider is decisive as they possess a vast understanding of the relevance of monitoring, which is indeed necessary for optimal website performance.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It helps you offer a seamless and positive experience that helps you ensure your customers come back and that your website maintains consistency in terms of user engagement.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Improve Brand Image\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Remember a website is the face of any business. It reflects much about businesses in terms of their philosophy and of course their offerings.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Moreover, a fully-functionality and easy-to-use website impresses visitors a lot and makes them feel good while accessing it. And it also encourages them to visit again and again.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>On the other hand, if your business has a poorly maintained website accompanied by broken links, various errors, dead pages, etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It’s certainly difficult for visitors to stay on your website for a longer time and you will find the deteriorated performance of your website that also impacts the growth of your business.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The main benefit of hiring a website maintenance company is they make a proper routine to analyze your website and also update the same when it comes to matching your corporate image.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>They thoroughly check every issue be its poor grammar, broken links, or others. And fix the same immediately without any hindrance.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"7.  Improve SEO Ranking\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Your business finds it tough to compete online without ranking on top in search engines. If you don’t update your website on a regular basis, you will fail to rank your website in Google and other search engines.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Even if your website already ranks, its ranking will fall without a proper update and maintenance of your website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Moreover, if your website’s content is not updated for a long time, it makes an adverse impact on search engine ranking. Google’s crawlers analyze the HTTP header of your website pages to decide whether crawling should be done.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A website maintenance service provider keeps eyes on all pages of your website and replaces the old content with new one.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>So, above are some of the advantages of website maintenance for small businesses. Simply having a website will not ensure the success of your business, no matter how good it is.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You need to constantly update your website with the latest trends and changing user behavior to help it stay relevant in the market. This is how website maintenance can helps small business with huge benefits.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Hire a reliable <a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/website-maintenance-company-bangalore/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">website maintenance service</a> provider that promises to deliver a world-class service.</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'Advantages Of Website Maintenance For Small Business', 'Every small Online Business must know the advantages of website maintenance for small business. Which can help them to compete with bigger brands easily.', '/uploads/blog/202410-1886c6fffae45d6e.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'website-maintenance'), 'published', '2024-10-16 03:23:30', '2024-10-16 03:23:30', '2025-02-28 05:02:51');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('top-6-ecommerce-website-maintenance-checklist', 'Top 6 eCommerce Website Maintenance checklist', 'Ecommerce web maintenance is a proactive approach to ensuring that your ecommerce website has no issues or downtime. It’s important to note that this isn’t just about fixing problems when they arise …', 'What is Ecommerce website Maintenance?\n\nEcommerce web maintenance is a proactive approach to ensuring that your ecommerce website has no issues or downtime. It’s important to note that this isn’t just about fixing problems when they arise but also preventing them before they happen. we have listed top ecommerce website maintenance checklist to help businesses/\n\nAs such, all organizations must invest in this type of service if they want their online store to perform well. This is why it’s important to find an experienced team of professionals who can manage your eCommerce web maintenance needs.\n\nDo you have a team of developers that can manage everything from code updates and security patches to database optimization? Or do you need someone to manage your hosting and server-level tasks?\n\nChoosing the right level of service can help ensure that your eCommerce website is always up-to-date and running smoothly.\n\nRelated Links:\n\nWebsite Speed Optimization : 5 Best Tips\n\nTop 6 Ecommerce Website Maintenance Checklist\n\nThe online shopping industry is worth billions of dollars, so it’s no surprise that more and more business owners are trying to get in on the action. If you want your e-commerce website to stand out from the crowd, you’ll need to make sure it’s built according to best practices. Here’s a checklist for launching an e-commerce site:\n\n1. Choose the right design (responsive)\n\n1.  Responsive design\n2. Template/theme\n3. Framework (if you’re doing custom development)\n4. CMS (if you’re doing custom development)\n5. Hosting provider, domain name, and SSL certificate\n\nWhen it comes to ecommerce website development, you need the ecommerce developers that has an experienced team of developers and designers. While it is possible to get away with a sub-par website, or even a non-responsive one for your eCommerce store, we recommend that you aim for perfection. You should always be striving for the best user experience possible and this starts with your design.\n\n2. Create a clear navigation system\n\nA clear navigation system is essential for any eCommerce website. The best way to do this is to use a menu bar at the top of your site and make sure it links to every page on your site, including categories, subcategories, and products.\n\nA sitemap (or table of contents) is another great way to help visitors navigate your pages without having to scroll through them all. It gives visitors an overview of what’s on offer so they can quickly scan through and find what they’re looking for.\n\nSunsys develops navigation for websites. it works on the basis of the business requirement and provides a solution for it.\n\nA search bar should also be included somewhere on your site so that customers can easily find exactly what they need without having to browse through everything else first. If possible, make sure it includes autocomplete functionality so users don’t misspell their searches or have trouble typing long phrases into search bars without making mistakes along the way (which can cause frustration).This is onother most important checklist point for your ecommerce store maintenance.\n\n3. \nCreate contact forms, maps, and search options\n\nAlong with collecting data, a contact form helps you improve your customer service by providing an easy channel for communication. You can also use this form to gather feedback and identify any problems that exist on the site.\n\nSunsys helps you add contact forms to your website. Often, these forms are built into the website design using HTML or CSS code; however, they can be added later through third-party applications like Gravity Forms or Jetpack from WordPress (which has its own free version).\n\n4. Make sure your site is secure\n\nAll your customers are going to be worried about the safety of their personal information and other data, so you need to make sure that you’re using secure websites. If a customer doesn’t feel safe shopping on your site, they won’t come back!\n\nUse HTTPS instead of HTTP. This means that your website will use an SSL certificate (Secure Sockets Layer) which encrypts any data sent over the internet so that hackers can’t see it or steal it.\nHowever, we creates ecommerce website security that keep your customers’ information safe and sound. security is one of the crucial point in your maintenance of ecommerce website.\n\n5. SEO, SEO, SEO\n\nIf you want to build your eCommerce website for SEO (Search Engine Optimization), there are some basic things to consider.\n\nUse keywords in your title tags, meta descriptions, and alt tags. These can be found by using Google’s search console tool or a keyword research tool like SEM Rush.\nMeta descriptions should be 160 characters or less and include a call to action such as “buy now.” The SEO community has also recommended including the main keyword phrase in the first 100 characters of your description. sunsys creates websites that are search engine friendly. It helps you create an internet presence that attracts visitors.\nSchema markup can help you get indexed faster by defining what your content is about so that Google knows how to classify it for users who are searching for certain types of information on their site (like recipes).\nThese ecommerce store seo maintenance helps you to keep update on trends.\n\n6. Create a payment gateway\n\nIt’s important that you use a secure payment gateway, so your customers’ information is protected and private. You should also look for one that accepts a variety of payment options, like credit cards and PayPal.\n\nMake it easy to use: The easier it is for your customers to make a purchase online, the more likely they are to do so—which means you’ll receive higher sales numbers overall! So be sure that your website has simple navigation tools (such as drop-down menus) and clear product descriptions that explain what each item does in detail.\n\nSet up easily from the start: You don’t want any unnecessary hurdles in front of potential customers when it comes time for them to pay for their purchase; therefore, try finding an eCommerce provider or platform that makes setting up an account super easy from day one!\ncreate a secure payment gateway to ensure the safety of customers’ data. This technology uses encryption to protect data such as credit card numbers and personal information.\n\nConclusion\n\nMaintaining an eCommerce site is a lot of work, and it’s easy to get behind. There’s also the possibility of oversights or simply missing critical maintenance tasks. This ecommerce website maintenance checklist can help you stay on top of things and keep your site secure with minimal effort and energy.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"What is Ecommerce website Maintenance?\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Ecommerce web maintenance is a proactive approach to ensuring that your ecommerce website has no issues or downtime. It’s important to note that this isn’t just about fixing problems when they arise but also preventing them before they happen. we have listed top ecommerce website maintenance checklist to help businesses/</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As such, all organizations must invest in this type of service if they want their online store to perform well. This is why it’s important to find an experienced team of professionals who can manage your eCommerce web maintenance needs.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Do you have a team of developers that can manage everything from code updates and security patches to database optimization? Or do you need someone to manage your hosting and server-level tasks?</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Choosing the right level of service can help ensure that your eCommerce website is always up-to-date and running smoothly.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/website-speed-optimization-5-best-tips\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">Website Speed Optimization : 5 Best Tips</a></strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Top 6 Ecommerce Website Maintenance Checklist\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The online shopping industry is worth billions of dollars, so it’s no surprise that more and more business owners are trying to get in on the action. If you want your e-commerce website to stand out from the crowd, you’ll need to make sure it’s built according to best practices. Here’s a checklist for launching an e-commerce site:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Choose the right design (responsive)\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>1.  Responsive design<br>2. Template/theme<br>3. Framework (if you’re doing custom development)<br>4. CMS (if you’re doing custom development)<br>5. Hosting provider, domain name, and SSL certificate</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>When it comes to ecommerce website development, you need the ecommerce developers that has an experienced team of developers and designers. While it is possible to get away with a sub-par website, or even a non-responsive one for your eCommerce store, we recommend that you aim for perfection. You should always be striving for the best user experience possible and this starts with your design.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Create a clear navigation system\"},{\"type\":\"paragra