e your site is secure\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>All your customers are going to be worried about the safety of their personal information and other data, so you need to make sure that you’re using secure websites. If a customer doesn’t feel safe shopping on your site, they won’t come back!</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Use HTTPS instead of HTTP. This means that your website will use an SSL certificate (Secure Sockets Layer) which encrypts any data sent over the internet so that hackers can’t see it or steal it.<br>However, we creates ecommerce website security that keep your customers’ information safe and sound. security is one of the crucial point in your maintenance of ecommerce website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. SEO, SEO, SEO\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you want to build your eCommerce website for SEO (Search Engine Optimization), there are some basic things to consider.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Use keywords in your title tags, meta descriptions, and alt tags. These can be found by using Google’s search console tool or a keyword research tool like SEM Rush.<br>Meta descriptions should be 160 characters or less and include a call to action such as “buy now.” The SEO community has also recommended including the main keyword phrase in the first 100 characters of your description. sunsys creates websites that are search engine friendly. It helps you create an internet presence that attracts visitors.<br>Schema markup can help you get indexed faster by defining what your content is about so that Google knows how to classify it for users who are searching for certain types of information on their site (like recipes).<br>These ecommerce store seo maintenance helps you to keep update on trends.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Create a payment gateway\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It’s important that you use a secure payment gateway, so your customers’ information is protected and private. You should also look for one that accepts a variety of payment options, like credit cards and PayPal.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Make it easy to use: The easier it is for your customers to make a purchase online, the more likely they are to do so—which means you’ll receive higher sales numbers overall! So be sure that your website has simple navigation tools (such as drop-down menus) and clear product descriptions that explain what each item does in detail.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Set up easily from the start: You don’t want any unnecessary hurdles in front of potential customers when it comes time for them to pay for their purchase; therefore, try finding an eCommerce provider or platform that makes setting up an account super easy from day one!<br>create a secure payment gateway to ensure the safety of customers’ data. This technology uses encryption to protect data such as credit card numbers and personal information.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Maintaining an eCommerce site is a lot of work, and it’s easy to get behind. There’s also the possibility of oversights or simply missing critical maintenance tasks. This ecommerce website maintenance checklist can help you stay on top of things and keep your site secure with minimal effort and energy.</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'Top 6 Ecommerce Website Maintenance Checklist', 'As a ecommerce store owner every aspect of website should be secured and clean to get more customer. Here are some Top 6 Must know Ecommerce Website Maintenance Checklist to help you to make your site healthy.', '/uploads/blog/202410-e8200291063f9c9e.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'e-commerce'), 'published', '2024-10-16 03:26:30', '2024-10-16 03:26:30', '2025-02-28 04:38:46');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('website-speed-optimization-5-best-tips', 'Website Speed Optimization : 5 Best Tips', 'It is universally acknowledged that all of us live in an age hugely governed by the different facets of technology and therefore has to be understood from the very outset. The internet has truly chan…', 'What is Website Speed Optimization?\n\nIt is universally acknowledged that all of us live in an age hugely governed by the different facets of technology and therefore has to be understood from the very outset.\n\nThe internet has truly changed our lives in more ways than we can ever imagine and therefore, most of our lives are now spent contemplating the different facets of websites and how to make their best use. This is seen to be relevant in multiple cases and various niches.\n\nSpeed is of utmost importance here, and when a website has proper speed, website speed optimization becomes easier and in the long run, working on those facets becomes feasible.\n\nReports by Google, Amazon, and others have reliably shown that quick website loading speed is one of the main components of site achievement: one review by the Aberdeen Group showed each 1-second postponement in page loading time prompted an 11% diminishing in online visits and 7% misfortune in changes.\n\nOf course, there are numerous ways you can upgrade your site for better execution, yet here are some speedy tips you can do now to develop your web execution and page load time\n\nRelated Links:\n\nTop 6 eCommerce Website Maintenance checklist\n\nTop 5 Tips For Website Speed Optimization\n\n1. Do A Fast, Free Investigation of Your Page Speed\n\nApparatuses, for example, Web Page Test, will show you precisely setting aside the longest effort to stack on your website page. Essentially enter the URL of the page you’re hoping to assess and trust that the outcomes will come in. For example, the underneath test is for the landing page of magnificence store Sephora: more than 200 components make up this page, and by checking out the left section, you can see what is setting aside the longest effort to stack. For instance, while the pictures take under 50 milliseconds to stack, a Facebook module takes 182 ms. Figuring out how to peruse a site page test is very important: discover more in our investigation of the speed of 300+ Magento sites.\n\n2.  Guarantee Your Pictures Are Improved for Web\n\nUtilize a picture-altering apparatus, for example, Photoshop or a free picture re-sizer, to measure your pictures suitably, so you’re not causing clients to download huge documents.\n\nTo do this, first, discover what the greatest permitted picture size is for your page or blog format, as a rule, it will not be more than 800px width, and regardless of whether you transfer bigger pictures, they will be estimated down. Then, the notion of web design has to be done accordingly.\nAssuming you use HTML tags, for example, and a width or tallness detail, you’re not lessening the picture size on your server, just how it shows up on the page.\n\nWhen you decide on your ideal picture size, save as that size. Assuming you’re utilizing a picture manager, you can likewise save at 80% quality, decreasing the record size.\n\nYou can choose choices that reduce the document size by your ideal rate (we don’t suggest saving over half more modest).\n\nJPG and PNG are the best record types for the web. This is one of the best web page speed opimization tip.\n\n3.  Decrease The Number of Modules on Your Site\n\nModules like Google Analytics give significant data; however, they can dial back page load time. These instruments typically work by entering a JavaScript bit someplace in your site code (usually in the header area).\n\nClients need to gather this remote record before the page is completely stacked when the client visits your page.\n\nAssuming that you have a few of these snippets, say one for Google Analytics, one for sharing on Facebook, and one for sharing on Twitter, your page will take more time to get done with stacking.\n\nSo, check your HTML code routinely to ensure you need all the modules introduced on your page.\n\n4. Eliminate Superfluous Code in Your CSS Records\n\nYour CSS document needs to stack before your page becomes visible; however, if you (and others) have been expanding upon a similar record for quite a while, it probably has a ton of unnecessary code – each additional room or line will amount to a slower pace! This will greatly help in the notion of web development. Go through the code yourself on the off chance that any secret components aren’t being utilized, or utilize a free CSS minified, which will eliminate additional areas and code for you. Here are a few assets Google proposes for minifying HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code. This can increase website speed.\n\n5. Store Your Pages\n\nYou drastically decrease the number of solicitations to your server by storing your pages, accelerating page load time, and reserving assists likewise with the versatility of your site during top traffic times, for example, when you are running an email advertising effort or online business deal.\n\nConclusion\n\nTo sum up, the range of potential options that can be explored here is thus found to be huge. Here we explored only five factors that can improve the overall website speed optimization.In this regard, it must be mentioned here that there are many other such ways to ensure that the tactics work perfectly.Websites govern many aspects of our lives, and thus, timely action and choosing the Best website maintenance company are needed to ensure that speed is always up to the best possible mark.The potential for future uses shall be then found to be huge and has to be therefore noted with due concern as well as diligence to be seen in this case.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"he