\"items\":[\"Highly Flexible\",\"Extensive Themes\",\"Open-Source Platform\",\"In-Built Payment\",\"Larger Library of Extensions\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Price:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"$20 to $100/ year\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"8. UpdraftPlus\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It’s one of the leading WP plugins that provides both automated and scheduled backup solutions for a range of options that include email, Google Drive, Dropbox, and many more. It’s easy to install. The configuration of the plugin doesn’t require much time. The credit goes to its backup and restoration feature. Since backup is stored in the dashboard, you can avail of the option to access them later.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Features:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Fully Comprehensive\",\"Easy to Use\",\"Highly Reliable\",\"Remote Storage Option\",\"Easy Migration of Website\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Price:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"$195/year\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"9. Akismet\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Akismet is another WP plugin that is a good option for those who are looking for an antispam plugin. It works better in evaluating all types of comments to filter out those various spam comments. This plugin can also check the URLs in the comments. It can remove various suspicious links as well. It includes a highly advanced security solution apart from anti-spam protection.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Features:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Monitor comments and removes spam\",\"Display only genuine comments\",\"Advanced Spam Statistics\",\"Privacy &amp; GDPR Compliance\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Price:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"$36/year\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"10. Redirection\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As the name suggests, this plugin works effectively when it comes to monitoring 301 redirects and 404-error. It’s a go-to plugin that is good for tracking those broken links and also various orphan pages. It brings the possibility for you to auto-track viewers of all types of URLs or also those of manually embed 302/307 redirects.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Features:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Easy to Install\",\"Redirect Logs\",\"Automated Redirect\",\"Manual Redirect\",\"Redirection by Logged-in Users\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Price:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"N/A\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can leverage the potential advantages of WordPress only if you use the best plugins. It’s crucial to select the best plugins based on the type of functionality you wish to add to your website.</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'Top 10 Must-Have WordPress Plugins For Your Business', 'Using the best WordPress plugins helps you add the desired functionality to your website. Choose the best one for your website based on your needs.', '/uploads/blog/202410-fb400b6e0dfba630.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'wordpress'), 'published', '2024-10-16 03:35:30', '2024-10-16 03:35:30', '2025-02-28 04:30:58');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('top-10-things-to-consider-before-hiring-wordpress-development-company', 'Top 10 Things to Consider Before Hiring WordPress Development Company', 'WordPress is the world’s most widely used CMS(Content management system), powering over half of all websites. But that doesn’t mean you should choose anyone who offers a WordPress website as part of …', 'Overview\n\nWordPress is the world’s most widely used CMS(Content management system), powering over half of all websites. But that doesn’t mean you should choose anyone who offers a WordPress website as part of their services.\n\nIf you don’t know what you’re doing, hiring a bad WordPress developer could be disastrous for your business and brand.\n\nIf you think to choosing a WordPress development agency is a tough task, you need to consider various factors. These will definitely make your task easy.so here are some top 10 tips to hire WordPress web development company.\n\nRelated Links:\n\nHow to Secure WordPress Website?\n\nList of Top 10 Tips to Hire WordPress Web Development Company\n\n1. Portfolio\n\nWhen you are looking to hire WordPress development company, the portfolio is an important factor that you should consider.\n\nIf a WordPress web development agency has a well-organized portfolio, it shows that the company is professional and has been in business for years.\n\nIf a WordPress web development agency shows off its skills with its works, it demonstrates its expertise.\n\nIf you see multiple projects in their portfolio, then it means that they have worked on different types of projects which can help them work on your project as well.\n\n2. Case studies\n\nCase studies are a great place to start when you’re looking for a WordPress website development. These show the quality of work you can expect, which is important because there are many skills and services that can be provided by these agencies.\n\nIf you see case studies from other clients where they have been happy with the results, this is a good indication that your project will go well too.\n\nYou may even get some ideas on how to improve certain aspects of your site or business! This article will helps for your “how to choose WordPress web development company?“\n\n3. Industry Experience\n\nThe most important thing to consider is the company’s experience. You want to work with an agency that has been in business for at least three years, and preferably longer.\n\nThis indicates that they have established themselves as experts in their field. If a company can’t demonstrate its expertise through client testimonials and case studies, stay away!\n\n4. Communication Skills\n\nCommunication is the key to success. It is important for any profession, but especially for web development companies. If you are looking to develop a website, it is imperative that you choose an agency with good communication skills.\n\n5. Name and Reputation of the Company\n\nReputation is the most important thing that you should check before hiring a WordPress website development agency. You have to make sure that the company has a good reputation in the industry.\n\nYou can find out about their credibility by checking reviews on Google, Facebook, and other websites where people usually leave comments after dealing with them.\n\nLook for WordPress web design & development companies that have been in this business for some time now as they will definitely be able to understand your requirements more clearly than a startup agency or freelancer out there.\n\n6. Knowledge of WordPress Plugin\n\nWordPress plugins are powerful tools that can be used to extend the functionality of your website. If the agency you are considering doesn’t know how to use WordPress plugins, they will not be able to help you with many of the tasks that require them.\n\nFor example, if you want a contact form on your site or a blog subscription option in your sidebar, these things require special WordPress plugins and it’s up to the agency to know how they work and where they can be found.\n\n7.  Website Optimization Methods\n\nYou will want to make sure that the web development agency you hire has experience in search engine optimization or SEO. SEO is a collection of methods used to increase the amount of traffic and visibility in search engines for your website.\n\nThere are many different techniques that can be used to improve your rankings on Google or other search engines, but they all fall into two main categories: on-page optimization, and off-page optimization.\n\nYou should also make sure that your potential web development partner has experience with analytics tools such as Google Analytics, which measures how users interact with websites and provides reports detailing where visitors came from, how long they stayed on each page, what pages were most popular among visitors (and which weren’t), etc.\n\n8. Website Designing Skills\n\nWebsite design is a critical part of any website. The web design skills of a WordPress development company are crucial to a successful project, and their ability to deliver what you want can make or break the success of your site.For SEO, it’s important that they know how search engines work, so they can optimize your website for search engines like Google and Bing. For UX (user experience), it’s important that they understand how users interact with websites so that they can create an intuitive interface that makes sense for your customer base.Finally, good web design is essential for making your site stand out from other sites in its industry—nothing attracts customers like attention-grabbing graphics and interesting page layouts!\n\n9. Team and Project Management Expertise\n\nWhen you’re choosing WordPress web development company, it’s important that the team has the experience and expertise required to deliver your project on time and on budget.\n\nThe best web development companies know this, which is why they have teams of certified professionals in place who have worked with clients before.\n\nA good WordPress company should have experienced developers that can handle any task assigned to them (from small bug fixes to complex customizations).\n\nThey should also understand how to communicate with clients effectively and be able to work independently without your constant supervision.\n\nKnowledge of WordPress Plugin\n\n1. Client Testimonials and Reviews\n\nBefore you hire any WordPress development agency, make sure to look at their client testimonials and reviews. Client feedback can be a good indicator of how the agency works with clients and if they are able to deliver what they promise.\n\nAlso, check for client referrals on social media, forums, or other platforms where people discuss web development agencies. These above mentioned tips to hire WordPress developers helps to select the best one.\n\nConclusion\n\nThis article is a compilation of all the things you should consider before hiring best WordPress agency It will help make your decision easier and give you more confidence in your choice.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Overview\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>WordPress is the world’s most widely used CMS(Content management system), powering over half of all websites. But that doesn’t mean you should choose anyone who offers a WordPress website as part of their services.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you don’t know what you’re doing, hiring a bad WordPress developer could be disastrous for your business and brand.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you think to choosing a WordPress development agency is a tough task, you need to consider various factors. These will definitely make your task easy.so here are some top 10 tips to hire WordPress web development company.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/how-to-secure-wordpress-website\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">How to Secure WordPress Website?</a></strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"List of Top 10 Tips to Hire WordPress Web Development Company\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Portfolio\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>When you are looking to hire WordPress development company, the portfolio is an important factor that you should consider.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If a WordPress web development agency has a well-organized portfolio, it shows that the company is professional and has been in business for years.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If a WordPress web development agency shows off its skills with its works, it demonstrates its expertise.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you see multiple projects in their portfolio, then it means that they have worked on different types of projects which can help them work on your project as well.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Case studies\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Case studies are a great place to start when you’re looking for a WordPress website development. These show the quality of work you can expect, which is important because there are many skills and services that can be provided by these agencies.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you see case studies from other clients where they have been happy with the results, this is a good indication that your project will go well too.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You may even get some ideas on how to improve certain aspects of your site or business! This article will helps for your “how to choose WordPress web development company?“</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Industry Experience\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The most important thing to consider is the company’s experience. You want to work with an agency that has been in business for at least three years, and preferably longer.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>This indicates that they have established themselves as experts in their field. If a company can’t demonstrate its expertise through client testimonials and case studies, stay away!</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Communication Skills\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Communication is the key to success. It is important for any profession, but especially for web development companies. If you are looking to develop a website, it is imperative that you choose an agency with good communication skills.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Name and Reputation of the Company\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Reputation is the most important thing that you should check before hiring a WordPress website development agency. You have to make sure that the company has a good reputation in the industry.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can find out about their credibility by checking reviews on Google, Facebook, and other websites where people usually leave comments after dealing with them.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Look for WordPress web design &amp; development companies that have been in this business for some time now as they will definitely be able to understand your requirements more clearly than a startup agency or freelancer out there.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Knowledge of WordPress Plugin\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>WordPress plugins are powerful tools that can be used to extend the functionality of your website. If the agency you are considering doesn’t know how to use WordPress plugins, they will not be able to help you with many of the tasks that require them.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>For example, if you want a contact form on your site or a blog subscription option in your sidebar, these things require special WordPress plugins and it’s up to the agency to know how they work and where they can be found.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"7.  Website Optimization Methods\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You will want to make sure that the web development agency you hire has experience in search engine optimization or SEO. SEO is a collection of methods used to increase the amount of traffic and visibility in search engines for your website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>There are many different techniques that can be used to improve your rankings on Google or other search engines, but they all fall into two main categories: on-page optimization, and off-page optimization.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You should also make sure that your potential web development partner has experience with analytics tools such as Google Analytics, which measures how users interact with websites and provides reports detailing where visitors came from, how long they stayed on each page, what pages were most popular among visitors (and which weren’t), etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"8. Website Designing Skills\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Website design is a critical part of any website. The web design skills of a WordPress development company are crucial to a successful project, and their ability to deliver what you want can make or break the success of your site.For SEO, it’s important that they know how search engines work, so they can optimize your website for search engines like Google and Bing. For UX (user experience), it’s important that they understand how users interact with websites so that they can create an intuitive interface that makes sense for your customer base.Finally, good web design is essential for making your site stand out from other sites in its industry—nothing attracts customers like attention-grabbing graphics and interesting page layouts!</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"9. Team and Project Management Expertise\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>When you’re choosing WordPress web development company, it’s important that the team has the experience and expertise required to deliver your project on time and on budget.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The best web development companies know this, which is why they have teams of certified professionals in place who have worked with clients before.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A good WordPress company should have experienced developers that can handle any task assigned to them (from small bug fixes to complex customizations).</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>They should also understand how to communicate with clients effectively and be able to work independently without your constant supervision.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"Knowledge of WordPress Plugin\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Client Testimonials and Reviews\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Before you hire any WordPress development agency, make sure to look at their client testimonials and reviews. Client feedback can be a good indicator of how the agency works with clients and if they are able to deliver what they promise.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Also, check for client referrals on social media, forums, or other platforms where people discuss web development agencies. These above mentioned tips to hire WordPress developers helps to select the best one.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>This article is a compilation of all the things you should consider before hiring best WordPress agency It will help make your decision easier and give you more confidence in your choice.</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'Top 10 Tips to Hiring WordPress Development Company', 'Here are some top 10 tips to hiring WordPress development company. As a business owner we get so many questions while choosing best company to develop our website.', '/uploads/blog/202410-37702473c433a1b3.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'wordpress'), 'published', '2024-10-16 03:36:58', '2024-10-16 03:36:58', '2025-02-27 12:57:58');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('how-to-secure-wordpress-website', 'How to Secure WordPress Website?', 'More than 29% of the web is powered by WordPress. With so many WordPress sites out there, the CMS is a frequent target for malicious practitioners. While this type of cybersecurity threat can be scar…', 'Overview\n\nMore than 29% of the web is powered by WordPress. With so many WordPress sites out there, the CMS is a frequent target for malicious practitioners. While this type of cybersecurity threat can be scary, you can secure your website by taking some necessary precautions. If you have question like “How to secure wordpress website?” After launching your site, Here are 8 ways to keep your site safe from attacks:\n\nRelated Links:\n\nTop 10 Things to Consider Before Hiring WordPress Development Company\n\nTop 8 Ways to Secure WordPress Website\n\n1.  Update WordPress\n\nIt’s important to keep your WordPress software up-to-date. To do this, you’ll need to:\n\n1. Install the latest version of WordPress\n\n2. Update your plugins and themes as well\n\n3. Check for new core releases on a regular basis\n\nYou can update the core by using the admin area of your site or downloading it from the WordPress website and uploading it manually. You should always use the latest security release of WordPress, which is called the Latest Security Release.\n\nIf you’d like more control over what gets updated, you can also choose which version gets updated with these options: Latest Minor Release, Latest Major Release, or Latest Patch Release.\n\n2. Secure your .htaccess file\n\nThe .htaccess file is a configuration file that allows you to make changes to your website’s HTTP server configuration. It’s important to secure this file because it contains sensitive information, including your database password, which could be used by hackers if they gain access.\n\nOnce you have access to the .htaccess file, you can edit it and change its permissions so they are more secure. Then, if anyone tries to access the file in their browser or through FTP software like FileZilla, they will be denied access unless they use an account with admin privileges.\n\n3. Password Protection\n\nTo protect WordPress website from hackers and other threats, you will want to set up a password-protected directory. The easiest way to do this is by adding a password through the user profile area of your WordPress dashboard.\n\nOnce you are logged into your WordPress dashboard, go to “Users” > “Edit” next to each username/login account you wish to protect with a password. You can then add an additional layer of security by adding one or more passwords:\n\n1. Add a password for admin access (typically found under Settings > General)\n\n2. Add a login name and password for accessing wp-admin (the directory containing all files related to administration)\n\n3. Add another login name and password for accessing wp-login.php\n\n4. A third possible login name and password that protects wp-config.php\n\nThe same procedure applies if there are multiple users on one website; just make sure they all have unique usernames so they don’t share the same account!\n\n4. Disable File Editing\n\nTo disable file editing, you can use the File Editing Restrictions plugin. To do this, follow these steps:\n\n1. Log into your WordPress Dashboard.\n2. Go to Plugins > Add New and search for File Editing Restrictions. Install and activate it. (If you’re using another method of installing plugins, follow those instructions.)\n3. Once installed and activated, go to Settings > File Editing Restrictions. Set the time frame in which users are allowed to edit files on your site as well as which types of files they can edit (such as images).\n\nYou can also configure this plugin with an option that allows users to request access for a particular file type at any time; just enter their email address in the “Special Requests” field on this page2..\n\n5. Limit Login Attempts\n\nThe WordPress database has a setting that allows you to set the number of login attempts before your account is reset. You can change this by going to Dashboard > Users > Your Profile and changing the Login Attempts field in the General tab.\n\nYou should also create a backup e-mail address for your account so that if you do get locked out, you can still regain access to your website.\n\n6. Two Factor Authentication\n\nBy using two-factor authentication, or 2FA, you can ensure that only users with the correct login credentials can access your WordPress site and its content.\n\nTo set up two-factor authentication on your WordPress site:\n\n1. Go to “Users” in the left sidebar of your dashboard. In the right column, click on “Add new user.”\n2. Fill out all fields and make sure you check off “Enable Two-Factor Authentication” near the bottom.\n3. Click “Add User” at the bottom of the page when finished.\n4. On this page, you will see a QR code that allows us to generate an authentication key from any device with a camera (phone or tablet).\n\nAfter generating this key we will be able to use it as an authenticator for logging into our WordPress account from another device in addition to typing in our password as before — making it much more difficult for someone else who does not have physical access to our devices being used for authentication purposes such as web browsers, etc., which would otherwise allow them unlimited access via traditional means such as brute force attacks using various combinations of username/password combinations until one matches what someone else knows about yours!\n\n7. Disable Directory Browsing and Error Reporting\n\nDirectory Browsing:\n\nDisable directory browsing to prevent access to your files. This can be done in WHM’s Security Center.\n\nTo disable this feature, simply click on the “Disable Directory Browsing” link near the top of the page and choose Yes when prompted to disable it.\n\nError Reporting:\n\nYou don’t want hackers using error reporting for their own gain because it can reveal files that are accessible through WordPress.\n\nTo disable error reporting, go into your php My Admin account (it may be different than cPanel) and find the wp-config.php file in your database directory and add this line: define( ‘WP_DEBUG’, false );\n\nConclusion\n\nWe hope you enjoyed reading this article and were able to take away some tips on how to keep your WordPress site safe. Remember that if your site is compromised, not only can it cost you time and money but also compromise your brand or reputation.\n\nFollow these steps to make sure you’re WordPress Security is protected from the most common attacks so that nothing goes wrong with your business’s online presence', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Overview\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>More than 29% of the web is powered by WordPress. With so many WordPress sites out there, the CMS is a frequent target for malicious practitioners. While this type of cybersecurity threat can be scary, you can secure your website by taking some necessary precautions. If you have question like “How to secure wordpress website?” After launching your site, Here are 8 ways to keep your site safe from attacks:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/top-10-things-to-consider-before-hiring-wordpress-development-company\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">Top 10 Things to Consider Before Hiring WordPress Development Company</a></strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Top 8 Ways to Secure WordPress Website\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1.  Update WordPress\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It’s important to keep your WordPress software up-to-date. To do this, you’ll need to:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>1. Install the latest version of WordPress</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>2. Update your plugins and themes as well</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>3. Check for new core releases on a regular basis</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can update the core by using the admin area of your site or downloading it from the WordPress website and uploading it manually. You should always use the latest security release of WordPress, which is called the Latest Security Release.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you’d like more control over what gets updated, you can also choose which version gets updated with these options: Latest Minor Release, Latest Major Release, or Latest Patch Release.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Secure your .htaccess file\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The .htaccess file is a configuration file that allows you to make changes to your website’s HTTP server configuration. It’s important to secure this file because it contains sensitive information, including your database password, which could be used by hackers if they gain access.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Once you have access to the .htaccess file, you can edit it and change its permissions so they are more secure. Then, if anyone tries to access the file in their browser or through FTP software like FileZilla, they will be denied access unless they use an account with admin privileges.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Password Protection\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>To protect WordPress website from hackers and other threats, you will want to set up a password-protected directory. The easiest way to do this is by adding a password through the user profile area of your WordPress dashboard.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Once you are logged into your WordPress dashboard, go to “Users” &gt; “Edit” next to each username/login account you wish to protect with a password. You can then add an additional layer of security by adding one or more passwords:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>1. Add a password for admin access (typically found under Settings &gt; General)</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>2. Add a login name and password for accessing wp-admin (the directory containing all files related to administration)</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>3. Add another login name and password for accessing wp-login.php</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>4. A third possible login name and password that protects wp-config.php</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The same procedure applies if there are multiple users on one website; just make sure they all have unique usernames so they don’t share the same account!</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Disable File Editing\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>To disable file editing, you can use the File Editing Restrictions plugin. To do this, follow these steps:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>1. Log into your WordPress Dashboard.<br>2. Go to Plugins &gt; Add New and search for File Editing Restrictions. Install and activate it. (If you’re using another method of installing plugins, follow those instructions.)<br>3. Once installed and activated, go to Settings &gt; File Editing Restrictions. Set the time frame in which users are allowed to edit files on your site as well as which types of files they can edit (such as images).</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can also configure this plugin with an option that allows users to request access for a particular file type at any time; just enter their email address in the “Special Requests” field on this page2..</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Limit Login Attempts\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The WordPress database has a setting that allows you to set the number of login attempts before your account is reset. You can change this by going to Dashboard &gt; Users &gt; Your Profile and changing the Login Attempts field in the General tab.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You should also create a backup e-mail address for your account so that if you do get locked out, you can still regain access to your website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Two Factor Authentication\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>By using two-factor authentication, or 2FA, you can ensure that only users with the correct login credentials can access your WordPress site and its content.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>To set up two-factor authentication on your WordPress site:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>1. Go to “Users” in the left sidebar of your dashboard. In the right column, click on “Add new user.”<br>2. Fill out all fields and make sure you check off “Enable Two-Factor Authentication” near the bottom.<br>3. Click “Add User” at the bottom of the page when finished.<br>4. On this page, you will see a QR code that allows us to generate an authentication key from any device with a camera (phone or tablet).</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>After generating this key we will be able to use it as an authenticator for logging into our WordPress account from another device in addition to typing in our password as before — making it much more difficult for someone else who does not have physical access to our devices being used for authentication purposes such as web browsers, etc., which would otherwise allow them unlimited access via traditional means such as brute force attacks using various combinations of username/password combinations until one matches what someone else knows about yours!</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"7. Disable Directory Browsing and Error Reporting\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong>Directory Browsing:</strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Disable directory browsing to prevent access to your files. This can be done in WHM’s Security Center.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>To disable this feature, simply click on the “Disable Directory Browsing” link near the top of the page and choose Yes when prompted to disable it.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong>Error Reporting:</strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You don’t want hackers using error reporting for their own gain because it can reveal files that are accessible through WordPress.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>To disable error reporting, go into your php My Admin account (it may be different than cPanel) and find the wp-config.php file in your database directory and add this line: define( ‘WP_DEBUG’, false );</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>We hope you enjoyed reading this article and were able to take away some tips on how to keep your WordPress site safe. Remember that if your site is compromised, not only can it cost you time and money but also compromise your brand or reputation.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Follow these steps to make sure you’re WordPress Security is protected from the most common attacks so that nothing goes wrong with your business’s online presence</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'How to Secure WordPress Website? - Complete Guide', 'How to improve WordPress security is the question most of get when we build website using WordPress. Here are some of the most helpful tips to secure your WordPress website.', '/uploads/blog/202410-9f855ec4683d0153.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'wordpress'), 'published', '2024-10-16 03:38:58', '2024-10-16 03:38:58', '2025-02-27 12:56:07');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('top-10-woocommerce-payment-gateways-in-india', 'Top 10 WooCommerce Payment Gateways in India', 'If you are planning to develop an online store for your eCommerce business, you should be aware of various payment gateways. The reason is these payment gateways let sellers accept money online from …', 'Introduction\n\nIf you are planning to develop an online store for your eCommerce business, you should be aware of various payment gateways. The reason is these payment gateways let sellers accept money online from customers for the products that they buy. Woocommerce Payment gateways in India have a crucial role in online transactions. So, you need to find the best payment gateways to integrate into your eCommerce website to run your business smoothly.\n\nIt’s a good idea to integrate multiple payment gateways into your eCommerce website to let your customers make online transactions smoothly. Since the eCommerce business is on the boom of late, it also pushed up the demand for payment gateway.\n\nAs per Statista, the payment gateway market in India was projected up to $446.9 million in 2017 and can grow up to 1708.1million dollars in the year 2025.\n\nWell, the selection of payment gateways is certainly not the easiest task and one has to struggle a lot to choose the right one. If you also need to choose the right payment gateways for your online store, you are in the right place to gather the vital details.\n\nWe will make your task easy by letting you know some of the top WooCommerce payment gateways in India along with their features. It will help you understand the right options based on your needs.\n\nRelated Links:\n\nBest WooCommerce Plugins to Website Development\n\nWhat is WooCommerce Payment Gateway?\n\nWell, when it comes to the Woocommerce payment gateway, it’s an application service that generally authorized debit or credit card payments for online retailers, businesses, brick and clicks, and also those many traditional brick and mortar.\n\nIt brings the possibility of the transfer of various details between the Front End Processor and the payment portal. A payment gateway service includes the ability to automate payment transactions between both sellers and buyers.\n\nA payment gateway is a third-party service that is a system of computer processes, which works on the behalf of merchants through a highly secured internet connection.\n\nWith the help of Woocommerce payment gateway infrastructure, sellers accept debit, credit, and also several other forms of electronic payments.\n\nWhat are the Benefits of Using WooCommerce Payment Gateways in India?\n\nA smooth checkout process is something quite essential for your online store. Most of the time online users abandon shopping carts due to the complicated checkout process. WooCommerce payment gateways ensure a smooth checkout process by letting you avail yourself of numerous advantages.\n\n1. Automated Taxes\n\nThe most important advantage of such a payment gateway is it supports automatic taxes and also geolocation. With the automatic tax, you can display the exact and accurate cost of all products that you sell along with taxes. It enables your customers to see the prices regardless of their location.\n\n2. Facilitate All Types of Payment\n\nAnother advantage of this payment gateway is it enables sellers to accept and receive all types of payments including pay on delivery, bank transfer, check, etc. If you use any payment processor like Rapids, you can also use its WooCommerce Website payment gateway plugin.\n\n3. More Customization for Checkout Process\n\nIt helps you customize the checkout process in a way to help you witness more sales of your products. Whether you wish to serve domestic or overseas customers, the WooCommerce payment gateway caters to your needs.\n\n10 Best WooCommerce Payment Gateways in India (Updated list 2023)\n\nNow, let’s discuss here some of the payment gateways that you can integrate into your website. Take a look.\n\n1. Razorpay\n\nWhile talking about some of the best WooCommerce payment gateways in India, it’s good to start with Razorpay, which is already popular among several merchants. With this, merchants can accept different types of payment from a range of sources be it credit cards, debit cards, net banking digital wallets, or UPI.\n\nTo integrate it into your online store, you need to just accomplish a couple of steps. Besides, it’s also popular for having a clean dashboard that ensures a smooth transaction.\n\nFeatures:\n\nEasy to integrate\n100+ payment modes\nInvoice payments\nAPI-driven automation\n24/7 support\n\nPrice:\n\n2% for debit/credit, net banking, and UPI. And 3% on international cards, Amex Cards, EMI, etc.\n\n2. CCAvenue\n\nCCAvenue is another popular payment gateway that you can use to integrate into your online store. It enables you to accept all forms of payments in India. This payment method can support 200+ options for payment and is also capable of processing different currencies.\n\nAs an iFrame integrated, CCAvenue allows your customers to make payments even on the checkout. Besides, it also includes smart dynamic checkouts. It also offers various features such as marketing tools, dynamic even notifications, smart analysis, etc.\n\nFeatures:\n\nRecurring payment\nMobile payment\nInternational transaction\nFraud detection system\n24/7 support\n\nPrice:\n\n2% for domestic, 3% for international transactions, and 4% for Amex Diners Club/American Express.\n\n3. Instamojo\n\nWhen it comes to Instamojo, it’s absolutely a payment gateway in India that you can also consider using. It enables merchants to accept payment through credit or debit cards. Apart from this, it also accepts other types of payment as well such as wallets, net banking, IMPS, UPI transaction, EMI, NEFT, etc. This payment gateway gives customers an outstanding checkout experience.\n\nFeatures:\n\nRecurring payment\nEasy process for onboarding\nLive chat facility\n100+ payment modes\nElectronic invoice payment\n\nPrice:\n\nFree for RTGS/NEFT, 2% + Rs. 3 per transaction for debit and credit cards.\n\n4. PayPal\n\nApart from India, PayPal also lets you accept payments from across the world. In other words, it helps you globalize your business as well. With this payment gateway, you can get a kind of surety that you can get a fully safe, fast, and also easy transaction.\n\nBesides, it also offers many other features like free return shipping, 180-day buyer protection, confidentiality, etc. It also supports multiple currencies and has advanced features like uploading cheques through a smartphone camera.\n\nFeatures:\n\nEasy to integrate\nQuick Activation\nDedicated support\n100+ payment sources\nIndustry-based success rates\n\nPrice:\n\nFree for UPI,1.80% + GST for Netbanking, 1.55% + GST for Paytm Wallet, 1.85% + GST for Credit Card, and 2.65% for international or AMEX.\n\n5. Cashfree\n\nCashfree is known for having numerous features that ensure a seamless transaction. Similar to other WooCommerce payment gateway plugins, it provides complete support to different types of payment methods such as wallets, net banking, and others. It also supports bulk payments.\n\nThis payment gateway can support on-demand payouts, instant funds, and also recurring payments. It also offers bank account verification to let you get more details about customers. The major advantage of this payment gateway is it enables shoppers to transfer money even at the lowest transaction rate.\n\nFeatures:\n\nHighly secured\nFraud checking\nSet up is free\nEasy to configure\nInstant refund\n\nPrice:\n\n1.75% for Credit/Debit card and net banking, 2.5 per transaction for cardless\n\n6. PayUMoney\n\nPayUMoney is another one of the trusted and top-rated payment gateways in India. The majority of merchants use this plugin to accept payments. Some of the popular brands are Netflix, Bookmyshow, Airbnb, Cred, Redbus, and many others.\n\nA customized transaction rate is something that distinguishes this payment gateway from others. But, this option is available only if your business has above Rs. 10 L transactions on a monthly basis.\n\nIt’s PCI-DSS compliant with 128-bit encryption. It’s also popular for offering the highest success rates in the transaction since it includes built-in save card options, which facilitate customers to go for the full checkout process.\n\nFeatures:\n\nSupport for 100+ foreign currency\nDedicated account manager\nInvoice generation\nProcess multiple currencies\nInternational payment\n\nPrice:\n\n2% + GST for every transaction\n\n7. PayKun\n\nIf you are in search of a payment gateway in India with the lowest TDR, you can consider using none other than PayKun. This is the reason why it’s an appropriate option for freelancers, small business owners, and bloggers.\n\nIts main objective is to let sellers avail themselves of affordable payment gateway options. Many brands use this solution for accepting money. Some of these brands are WinTrust, Tryitfirst, iCure Diet Clinic, and others. It ensures a safe payment gateway and also ties up with many popular banks such as Yes Bank, ICICI bank, Paytm, Bill desk, and many others.\n\nPayKun also includes various payment links and buttons for quick transactions. Besides, it also offers free integration help and also a fully dedicated account manager, which is the other biggest advantage of using the same.\n\nFeatures:\n\nOutstanding support\n120+ payment modes\nQuick settlement\nAffordable cost\nAmazing check-out experience\n\nPrice:\n\n1.75% for a debit card, 2% for a credit card, 1.75% for net banking, and 3% for an international card.\n\n8. Stripe\n\nStripe is another option for a payment gateway solution that businesses can use. Whether you sell your products domestically or globally, you can do with the use of this payment gateway. It also accepts multiple currencies from different countries.\n\nStripe is also the most preferred choice among merchants for having a great UI and UX compared to other payment gateways such as Razorpay and many others. It also offers various other products such as pre-built payment pages that are appropriate for all types of businesses as well.\n\nFeatures:\n\nMobile customer interface\nDigital wallet integration\nMobile payment\nMulti-currency\nCredit card process\n\nPrice:\n\n2% for domestic cards and 3% for international cards\n\n9. PayGlocal\n\nIt’s another payment gateway solution that enjoys having a great reputation across the world. If you need a secure, fast, and reliable payment gateway that enables you to accept payment globally, you can go for none other than PayGlocal.\n\nIt offers world-class security that can be a wonderful choice for your business. It facilitates accepting payment from customers across the world and also helps you expand your business gradually. It supports international currency settlement as well.\n\nFeatures:\n\nSupport for multiple currencies\nMaintain transparency\nGreat protection from chargeback\nTransparent\nLocal Payment method\n\nPrice:\n\nN/A\n\n10. Billdesk\n\nIt’s one of the reliable payment gateways that you can use to experience a mind-blowing payment experience with customers. The credit goes to this payment system that enables customers to pay different bills such as ISP, electricity, phones, telephone, insurance, etc. Customers get a kind of surety of online transactions with SSL.\n\nFeatures:\n\nSecure payment gateway\nSupport for recurring payments\nEmail reminders on daily basis for bill payment\n24/7 support service\n\nPrice:\n\nN/A\n\nWhat Is Website Maintenance And Why It is Important?\n\nConclusion\n\nChoosing reliable payment gateways is something that not only helps customers make transactions smoothly but also improves their shopping experience. Above are some of the payment gateways that you can choose to integrate into your online store to make your online store successful.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Introduction\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you are planning to develop an online store for your eCommerce business, you should be aware of various payment gateways. The reason is these payment gateways let sellers accept money online from customers for the products that they buy. Woocommerce Payment gateways in India have a crucial role in online transactions. So, you need to find the best payment gateways to integrate into your eCommerce website to run your business smoothly.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It’s a good idea to integrate multiple payment gateways into your eCommerce website to let your customers make online transactions smoothly. Since the eCommerce business is on the boom of late, it also pushed up the demand for payment gateway.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As per Statista, the payment gateway market in India was projected up to $446.9 million in 2017 and can grow up to 1708.1million dollars in the year 2025.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Well, the selection of payment gateways is certainly not the easiest task and one has to struggle a lot to choose the right one. If you also need to choose the right payment gateways for your online store, you are in the right place to gather the vital details.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>We will make your task easy by letting you know some of the top WooCommerce payment gateways in India along with their features. It will help you understand the right options based on your needs.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/best-woocommerce-plugins-to-website-development\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">Best WooCommerce Plugins to Website Developme