refore, you need to make sure that your eCommerce store is mobile-friendly. It’s crucial to be focused more on visual elements rather than several text elements. It’s good to use various bullet points and also short copies where text is crucial. It’s also a great option to use video wherever possible.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"9. Offer Free Stuff\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You need to understand the fact that you should increase your business revenue by offering those several freebies. When it comes to free stuff, it’s helpful for long-term sales.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>For instance, free products are indeed quite helpful for creating customer reliability. You don’t need to give away those of your free things. You can also provide some free trials for giving customers some time for getting the value of products before they commit. You can also provide free shipping and also delivery on the purchase of your products beyond a certain amount for increasing the average value.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"10) Consistent Messaging\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Consistent messaging is another thing that you can do for increasing sales of eCommerce. If you maintain consistency in terms of logos, layouts, sales content, color, and various other communication elements, your customers can easily recognize your business.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>All you need to do is make certain strategies and also various tools for maintaining consistent messaging. Beginners can use various automated tools for integrating with their online store for creating various messaging templates. You can also make use of content management systems for sharing the content most efficiently with those of your brand identifiers across your eCommerce store.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"11. Chatbot\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A chatbot is doing wonderful and helps businesses in maintaining their customer support fully. And it’s directly related to sales of your products. It not just acts as a proper guide to customers but also ensures two-way communication and also creates a healthy relationship.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can integrate a chatbot into your online store for answering customers’ queries in terms of products and also facilitate shopping. Apart from this, you can also provide ‘human names’ to those of eCommerce chatbots for increasing engagement rates.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"12. Try Out Gmail Ads\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Gmail Promotion and Paid Gmail Ads are fully interactive advertisements displayed at the top of a prospect’s inbox in a fully promotional or social tab. You can also design those functional Gmail advertisements for promoting your online retail business in various ways. These options are vast.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>When it comes to prospects viewing Gmail Ads, these are the awareness and interest phases of the marketing funnel. Therefore, you should design and create your Gmail Ad copy like a landing page. You should make sure that you include a fully unique value proposition.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"13. Go Through Checkout Process\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The next thing that you need to do is increase eCommerce sales and review the checkout process from time to time. It helps you improve the user experience of your online store and thus, it brings a plethora of growth opportunities.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The more time customers spend putting personal information and payment details, the higher risk of cart abandonment rate they face.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>So, you need to make the checkout process easy and quick to encourage customers to complete the buying process.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"14. Upselling\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Upselling is another way of increasing eCommerce sales. Assume a case, where your customer accesses the checkout page and decides to shop for a particular product. And they get a recommendation for more appropriate products in a similar category and type. They will be lured to these products.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Upselling works a lot when it comes to increasing revenue and also establishing a long-term relationship with customers. It’s effective since the majority of selling is to a customer base that you already know.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"15. Get Paid Social Traffic\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Last but not least, social traffic will help you increase traffic to your online store, and thus, it pushes up sales. When you run a paid campaign, only your existing followers can visualize the same.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Paid advertisement helps reach a new audience if you wish to boost eCommerce sales. When it comes to social media platforms, these offer various extensive options for targeting the right people with fully sponsored content.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can target people based on their demographic, buying interest, gender, location, and more. These are the right factors that help you find your actual potential customers. You should always keep in mind that your paid campaigns don’t always have to be for your products.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Why most the Online Business don’t Get more Sales\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Even if you sell useful and top-quality products, you often fail to increase sales. There can be numerous reasons for the same. Some of these reasons are</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Unable to help Customers with Product Search\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You need to understand the fact that customers do a lot of research work before they make a final decision of buying products. Meanwhile, the most common reason why online stores face a tough time, customers may wish to do some research before they may purchase. If you are not capable of assisting customers with product research like linking with those articles and blog posts on the product page.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Poor Checkout Experience\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Customers nowadays hold a higher expectation towards a fully frictionless and also simple checkout experience. To match the expectation, many eCommerce businesses provide digital payment services that provide a higher level of security and simplicity.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Make sure your company offers various traditional payment options such as debit and credit cards.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Slow Page Loading Speed\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Slow loading speed is something that makes an adverse impact on user experience. It thus affects eCommerce sales as well. Even if customers want to buy your products, they will drop the idea of buying your products due to the slow loading speed of your website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Higher Abandonment Rate\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A higher abandonment rate is another reason for low eCommerce sales. It’s a fact that abandoned carts are the biggest concern of various merchants and also online retailers. So, you need to focus on the card abandonment rate and try to minimize the same if you want to increase sales of your products.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Lack of Social Proof\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Lack of social proof causes a decline in trust reliability, which adversely affects your business and its sales. Social proof also plays a vital role in increasing and also persuading customers to opt for your business and also place their final order. The lack of trust equals fewer sales and conversion.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>To make your business survive for a longer time while earning a huge profit, you should adopt various ways to increase eCommerce sales. Above are some of the strategies that you can implement to improve eCommerce sales.</p>\"}]}]}]}', '15 Effective Ways to Increase Ecommerce Sales', 'Do you want to increase sales of your eCommerce business? You need to always go with a rock solid strategy to witness the desired outcomes.', '/uploads/blog/202410-c21020de6324d125.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'e-commerce'), 'published', '2024-10-16 06:47:44', '2024-10-16 06:47:44', '2025-02-27 08:58:54');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('ecommerce-website-development-cost-complete-pricing-guide', 'eCommerce Website Development Cost Complete Pricing Guide', 'If you are running an eCommerce business, you may already be aware of the importance of a website. It not only highlights but also promotes and sells your products. It helps you in both sales and mar…', 'Introduction\n\nIf you are running an eCommerce business, you may already be aware of the importance of a website. It not only highlights but also promotes and sells your products. It helps you in both sales and marketing of the products that your organization deals with. Additionally, it ensures your 24/7 presence in the market. Though an online store runs any eCommerce business smoothly, still some entrepreneurs make mistakes and they often move ahead with an insufficient ecommerce website cost for investment. As a result, they get a less-performing website that doesn’t help their business in growth. So, whether you are planning to develop a new website or seeking to redevelop the existing one, you need to have a sufficient budget. Here are some tips to calculate ecommerce website development cost.\n\nRelated Links:\n\nTop 10 Benefits of eCommerce for Small Business\n\nTop 10 tips to scale ecommerce website development cost\n\nLet’s discuss here some valuable tips and tricks that you can implement to make a conversion-oriented website for your business and keep your business on the right path. Take a look at eCommerce website development cost\n\n1. Choosing an eCommerce Platform\n\nIt’s wise to start from the platform while talking about some of the factors that one should consider while planning for an eCommerce development cost. While developing an eCommerce store, the first thing that you do is to choose the right platform. And you need to be aware of the fact that the selection of an eCommerce platform has a great impact on the investment for eCommerce development.\n\nSome eCommerce platforms are free whereas others are fully paid. For instance, WooCommerce is a completely open-source platform. Meanwhile, you need to make some expenses for purchasing some necessary WooCommerce extension plugins.\n\nOn the other hand, Shopify is one of the leading platforms where you are liable to pay only for a Shopify account for creating your store. The most important advantage of this platform is that you will get a breakdown of the cost on a monthly basis for certain necessary features. On the other hand, some WooCommerce features generally need different types of development work.\n\n2. Development Cost\n\nThese are the actual expenses for eCommerce development. Most people are often curious to know about the overall cost of design and development of your eCommerce store. Well, the overall development cost of any project depends upon complications and also the scope of your website.\n\nBesides, the development cost also depends on the complexity of your projects. The cost of an eCommerce engine also makes a huge impact on the development of the online store. If you want to make your online store successful, you need to select eCommerce applications. It’s something that needs to include you for managing various customer loyalty functions, sharing information, maintaining customer relations, etc.\n\n3. Hosting eCommerce Website\n\nWhile searching for eCommerce website hosting services, you will come across different plans from different service providers. No matter which plans you opt for, you need to pay a hefty amount. All you need to do is make a selection of the right hosting service for your online store based on your budget.\n\nFor eCommerce hosting, you will get what you pay for. You will find several cheap hosting plans that claim good uptime records. But, you need to also understand the fact that eCommerce apps tend to be highly demanding. You must choose the right hosting company that hosts those other websites successfully.\n\n4. Template Vs Custom Design\n\nMost people find it hard to decide between template design and custom design. They don’t find the right option between them. To decide the right option between these, you need to consider completing the market, a timeline for the project, time to market, complexity, customization needs for products, etc.\n\nWhether you choose Shopify or WooCommerce for your eCommerce website development, you will find various pre-designed templates. You need to understand that customization of a new template can be a cost-effective option only if you have a new website. The reason is it minimizes teamwork. Apart from this, it can also minimize the timeline for creating a website if you want to take your products to the market quickly.\n\nWhen it comes to the custom design approach, it reflects that the designer crafts a mockup of your website completely from scratch. This is indeed the best option for those who are planning for a larger investment and seeking to get top-quality design.\n\n5. Payment Merchant\n\nA payment gateway is one of the crucial features of an eCommerce store that facilitates buyers to do online transactions successfully for products they buy. You need to understand that the choice of payment gateway also makes a great impact on your eCommerce development cost. You can get the three most popular options for payment gateways such as Paypal, Stripe, and Authorize.net\n\nWhether you select a WooCommerce or Shopify platform, you will get an option to integrate all these payment gateways. The processing fees for these gateways are 2.9% and also they charge an additional amount of $0.30 for every transaction. Besides, you also need to pay certain additional setup fees, which depend on your selection of the payment gateway.\n\n6. Product Images\n\nThe next thing that you need to invest in is the images of your products that you need to display on your online store. These images not only represent your products but also make your website appealing. If your organization doesn’t have a logo, you need to invest in having one created as a part of your marketing plan.\n\nMeanwhile, you need to understand that these images are not free. You need to use only original images of your products on your website. It helps you avoid any legal complications in the future.\n\nSo, you need to hire a professional photographer to get original pictures for your website. You can find them on a different budget. Therefore, you should hire them based on your ecommerce website cost.\n\n7. Content\n\nContent is one of the crucial things that determine the success of your eCommerce store. It informs users about products in detail, in terms of features and specifications. You need content for different categories of products, apart from Home Page, About Us, Privacy Policy, and others.\n\nSo, you need to choose content writing services, which also have an impact on the cost of eCommerce website development.\n\n8. Shipping Partner\n\nChoosing the right shipping partner for your eCommerce service is highly important. You can find various options while searching for shipping partners, including FedEx, DHL, Ekart, Blue Dart, eCom Express, and many more. These shipping partners have different charges. So, choosing them also makes a huge impact on your eCommerce website development cost.\n\n9. Maintenance Cost\n\nNo matter how advanced your eCommerce store is, it needs a regular website maintenance service. You get tools from your eCommerce engines that you require for managing your customers’ data, products, and promotions. eCommerce software often gets updated to offer various cutting-edge features and also boost security and various updates that you need to apply by those of many knowledgeable developers. It’s good to continue the partnership with your developers to get the required maintenance and support for your website.\n\n10. SSL Certificate\n\nNo matter what, the security of your online store is something that you are not supposed to compromise in any case. There are several ways you can use to secure your eCommerce website – implementing an SSL certificate is one of those ways.\n\nSome hosting plans are available with free SSL whereas others are available with paid SSL. So, it’s advisable to go through the complete hosting plan and then choose the right one accordingly.\n\nIf you choose a hosting plan that offers free security, it minimizes your investment.\n\nConclusion\n\nHope this Guide to eCommerce website development cost plan will help in reducing the budget burden. Do you still have any confusion in planning a budget for your eCommerce website? Well, if not, it’s time to involve active preparation for your online store development.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Introduction\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you are running an eCommerce business, you may already be aware of the importance of a website. It not only highlights but also promotes and sells your products. It helps you in both sales and marketing of the products that your organization deals with. Additionally, it ensures your 24/7 presence in the market. Though an online store runs any eCommerce business smoothly, still some entrepreneurs make mistakes and they often move ahead with an insufficient ecommerce website cost for investment. As a result, they get a less-performing website that doesn’t help their business in growth. So, whether you are planning to develop a new website or seeking to redevelop the existing one, you need to have a sufficient budget. Here are some tips to calculate ecommerce website development cost.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/top-10-benefits-of-ecommerce-for-small-business\\\" target=\\\"_blank\