/p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Well, when it comes to Clutch, it’s one of the reliable websites that you can go through to read the real reviews of clients about the company. It’s a reliable place that enables you to gather the real details about your service provider. It helps you find out if any recurrent issues in the process of projects are completed.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Another good advantage of using the clutch is it includes unbiased reviews written directly by clients. Clutch conducts genuine client review and creates verified profiles of service providers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Have a Look at their Website\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The next thing that you need to do is to get a complete overview of their website. It’s something that you need to do even before taking a look at their portfolio. Once you go through your service provider’s official website, it gives you idea terms of the responsibility and competence of your website. If they claim world-class eCommerce development services, then you can expect them to reflect the same thing through their website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Go through the CVs of their Professionals\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You should not forget to check the CVs of the professional team members working with the eCommerce development company that you wish to hire. Hiring a perfect team is indeed necessary for implementing a successful project.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you are in the consideration phase, you are suggested to ask your service provider to provide the CVs of the team members who are concerned about handling your projects. This is indeed the right way to find out if they have everything to deliver your projects successfully. Apart from this, it also gives you a kind of assurance that your project is in the right hands.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Check for Additional Services\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>When you develop an eCommerce website for your business, you need to always think of long-term solutions rather than short-term solutions. Besides, you should also take it from a broader perspective.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You need to understand that your website needs some extra services that include graphics designers, UX experts, and SEO professionals to take your development to another level. You need to choose a service that offers all the required services. And it will help you in saving various troubles. If you save time, it helps you in focusing on your core business needs and you will be able to grow your business.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Looks for Nearshoring or Offshoring\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The next thing that you need to be concerned about when hiring an eCommerce service provider is offshoring or nearshoring. In nearshoring, the software development company is located in neighboring countries. It indicates that you will be able to visit your eCommerce development company to interact face to face when required. This is the most crucial arrangement, especially if you have a large project to develop as it needs constant collaboration and feedback.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Offshoring, on the other hand, reflects that the eCommerce development company is located in another country. In this, the company is generally based in remote locations overseas. It naturally leads to a time zone difference, which makes quick fixes, or also real-time communication, which is certainly impossible. The positive side of offshoring is it helps you keep the development cost minimum.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>So, you need to make the right decision based on the type of your project to Choose The Best Ecommerce Development Company.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>When hiring an eCommerce development company, you will come across numerous options. All you need to do is choose and hire the best company that caters to your needs and delivers you the best website. Following the above tips for How to Find the Best eCommerce Development Company help you in making the right decision.</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'Best 6 Tips To Hire Best Ecommerce Web Design Company', 'Thinking to start ecommerce business and looking for best developers in the city? Here are tips to hire best ecommerce web design company.', '/uploads/blog/202410-5a45ded58d5849aa.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'e-commerce'), 'published', '2024-10-16 06:54:20', '2024-10-16 06:54:20', '2026-07-16 10:42:55');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('top-10-ecommerce-platforms', 'Top 10 eCommerce Platforms', 'eCommerce platforms are essential for any business that wants to take advantage of the online marketplace. Choosing the right one can be a daunting task, but we’ve got you covered with our list of th…', 'Introduction\n\neCommerce platforms are essential for any business that wants to take advantage of the online marketplace. Choosing the right one can be a daunting task, but we’ve got you covered with our list of the top 10 eCommerce platforms in 2023!\n\nRelated Links:\n\nHow to Build an Ecommerce website-Complete Guide\n\nTop 10 eCommerce Platforms\n\nIndian website development companies are popular for offering creative, powerful, and user-centric web solutions at the most competitive prices. We have discussed top website development companies in India that provide world class solutions.\n\n1. Shopify eCommerce Platform\n\nShopify is easy to set up and use, making it perfect for small businesses and entrepreneurs. It offers a wide range of features, including custom themes and extensions for further customization.\n\nPros:\n\nSimple to use\nShopify App Store\n24/7 support\n\nCons:\n\nComplicated blog post export\nPaid app required for AMP features\nNo option for multiple discounts\n\n2. WooCommerce – Best WordPress Plugin\n\nWooCommerce is the most popular eCommerce platform, known for its flexibility and a variety of integrations with other platforms, such as social media and payment processors. Pros:\n\nSimple to use\nShopify App Store\n24/7 support\n\nCons:\n\nComplicated blog post export\nPaid app required for AMP features\nNo option for multiple discounts\n\n3. BigCommerce – Complete eCommerce Website Builder\n\nBigCommerce can handle a large number of orders and offers an easy-to-use design, making it suitable for both novice and experienced users. Pros:\n\nLots of features\nProduct variants\nHigher scalability\n\nCons:\n\nLack of marketing tools\nYearly sales threshold\n\n4. Magento – Best for Large Businesses and Enterprises\n\nMagento is a powerful platform that is flexible and scalable, ideal for creating both large and small online stores. Pros:\n\nFlexible\nVast community support\nMany features\n\nCons:\n\nHighly expensive\nLimited number of developers\nTime-consuming to manage\n\n5. Volusion – eCommerce Website Builder\n\nVolusion features a drag-and-drop design, making it easy for users to create and manage their shopping carts, along with various integrations. Pros:\n\nSearch and filter options\nProduct catalog management\nBulk product uploads\n\nCons:\n\nNot user-friendly\nPoor customer service\nCode issues\n\n6. Squarespace – eCommerce Website Building Platform\n\nSquarespace is known for its user-friendly interface and drag-and-drop layout, allowing businesses to create websites quickly without prior web development knowledge. Pros:\n\nAvailable templates\nGreat for photography-based businesses\nEasy to use\n\nCons:\n\nExpensive pricing\nNo phone support\nEasy to use\n\n7. Prestashop – A Unique eCommerce Business Builder\n\nPrestashop has a user-friendly interface with built-in payment processing and merchandising tools, making it ideal for small businesses. Pros:\n\nEasy to install\nUser-friendly\nSimple customization\n\nCons:\n\nLimited scalability\nUnprofessional design options\nNo official support\n\n8. Wix – eCommerce Website Builder\n\nWix is a straightforward eCommerce platform that allows anyone to create a website quickly using a drag-and-drop editor. Pros:\n\nUpgraded design templates\nUseful and intuitive interface\nAll-in-one solutions\n\nCons:\n\nNo unlimited plan\nDrag-and-drop feature may limit creativity\nAds cannot be removed on the starter plan\n\n9. Weebly – eCommerce Platform\n\nWeebly is easy to set up and offers a wide range of features, along with a great support team for assistance. Pros:\n\nEasy drag-and-drop functionality\nMobile optimization\nExtensive website themes library\n\nCons:\n\nLimited blogging tools\nNot universally compatible\nPaid assistance for support\n\n10. 3DCart\n\n3DCart provides solutions tailored to business requirements and goals, allowing users to create customized online stores. Pros:\n\nEasy to use\nVariety of themes and templates\nIncludes web hosting\n\nCons:\n\nDifficult to navigate\nExpensive payment processing options\nLimited free themes\n\nWhat Is Website Maintenance And Why It is Important?\n\nConclusion\n\nWith eCommerce becoming increasingly popular, businesses have a variety of platforms to choose from when setting up their online store. This article outlines the top 10 eCommerce platforms in 2023, helping you to determine which one is right for your business.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Introduction\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>eCommerce platforms are essential for any business that wants to take advantage of the online marketplace. Choosing the right one can be a daunting task, but we’ve got you covered with our list of the top 10 eCommerce platforms in 2023!</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/how-to-build-an-ecommerce-website-complete-guide\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">How to Build an Ecommerce website-Complete Guide</a></strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Top 10 eCommerce Platforms\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Indian website development companies are popular for offering creative, powerful, and user-centric web solutions at the most competitive prices. We have discussed top website development companies in India that provide world class solutions.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Shopify eCommerce Platform\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Shopify is easy to set up and use, making it perfect for small businesses and entrepreneurs. It offers a wide range of features, including custom themes and extensions for further customization.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Simple to use\",\"Shopify App Store\",\"24/7 support\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Complicated blog post export\",\"Paid app required for AMP features\",\"No option for multiple discounts\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. WooCommerce – Best WordPress Plugin\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>WooCommerce is the most popular eCommerce platform, known for its flexibility and a variety of integrations with other platforms, such as social media and payment processors. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Simple to use\",\"Shopify App Store\",\"24/7 support\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Complicated blog post export\",\"Paid app required for AMP features\",\"No option for multiple discounts\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. BigCommerce – Complete eCommerce Website Builder\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>BigCommerce can handle a large number of orders and offers an easy-to-use design, making it suitable for both novice and experienced users. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Lots of features\",\"Product variants\",\"Higher scalability\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Lack of marketing tools\",\"Yearly sales threshold\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Magento – Best for Large Businesses and Enterprises\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Magento is a powerful platform that is flexible and scalable, ideal for creating both large and small online stores. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Flexible\",\"Vast community support\",\"Many features\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Highly expensive\",\"Limited number of developers\",\"Time-consuming to manage\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Volusion – eCommerce Website Builder\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Volusion features a drag-and-drop design, making it easy for users to create and manage their shopping carts, along with various integrations. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Search and filter options\",\"Product catalog management\",\"Bulk product uploads\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Not user-friendly\",\"Poor customer service\",\"Code issues\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Squarespace – eCommerce Website Building Platform\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Squarespace is known for its user-friendly interface and drag-and-drop layout, allowing businesses to create websites quickly without prior web development knowledge. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Available templates\",\"Great for photography-based businesses\",\"Easy to use\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Expensive pricing\",\"No phone support\",\"Easy to use\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"7. Prestashop – A Unique eCommerce Business Builder\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Prestashop has a user-friendly interface with built-in payment processing and merchandising tools, making it ideal for small businesses. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Easy to install\",\"User-friendly\",\"Simple customization\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Limited scalability\",\"Unprofessional design options\",\"No official support\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"8. Wix – eCommerce Website Builder\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Wix is a straightforward eCommerce platform that allows anyone to create a website quickly using a drag-and-drop editor. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Upgraded design templates\",\"Useful and intuitive interface\",\"All-in-one solutions\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"No unlimited plan\",\"Drag-and-drop feature may limit creativity\",\"Ads cannot be removed on the starter plan\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"9. Weebly – eCommerce Platform\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Weebly is easy to set up and offers a wide range of features, along with a great support team for assistance. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Easy drag-and-drop functionality\",\"Mobile optimization\",\"Extensive website themes library\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Limited blogging tools\",\"Not universally compatible\",\"Paid assistance for support\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"10. 3DCart\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>3DCart provides solutions tailored to business requirements and goals, allowing users to create customized online stores. Pros:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Easy to use\",\"Variety of themes and templates\",\"Includes web hosting\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Cons:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"Difficult to navigate\",\"Expensive payment processing options\",\"Limited free themes\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/what-is-website-maintenance-and-why-it-is-important\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">What Is Website Maintenance And Why It is Important?</a></p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>With eCommerce becoming increasingly popular, businesses have a variety of platforms to choose from when setting up their online store. This article outlines the top 10 eCommerce platforms in 2023, helping you to determine which one is right for your business.</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'Top 10 Ecommerce Platforms in 2023', 'In a growing digital market ecommerce business has made tremendous increase. you may be confused with which ecommerce platform you have to choose for your business. don\'t worry We have listed most popular and top 10 ecommerce platforms in 2023.', '/uploads/blog/202410-523a1f6e33d74839.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'e-commerce'), 'published', '2024-10-16 07:01:23', '2024-10-16 07:01:23', '2025-02-27 08:53:02');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('5-things-to-consider-before-starting-an-ecommerce-business', '5 Things to Consider Before Starting an Ecommerce Business', 'You may have heard people saying ‘Do what you love and the money will follow’ or ‘Build your passion and then pursue it full-time’. While these phrases may be true for some, today’s reality is that e…', 'Overview\n\nYou may have heard people saying ‘Do what you love and the money will follow’ or ‘Build your passion and then pursue it full-time’. While these phrases may be true for some, today’s reality is that entrepreneurship can come with many challenges.\n\nOne of them is financial security. Creating a new business is a risky endeavor and there are no guarantees that it will be successful. But if you plan in advance before starting your eCommerce business you can minimize the risk. An E-commerce web design agency’s suggests the top 5 things to consider before starting an eCommerce business:\n\nRelated Links:\n\n5 Things to Consider Before Starting an Ecommerce Business\n\n5 Things You Need to Know Before Starting an eCommerce Business\n\n1. Knowing your Niche\n\nA niche is a small group of people with a shared interest in something specific. The more focused your niche, the better you can serve them and the more money you will make. Many E-commerce website development companies recommend this point. Knowing your niche is the first step toward starting an eCommerce business.\n\nIf you want to start your own eCommerce business, you need to know about the product, market, and competitors in detail. Knowing your niche helps you to focus on a particular segment of the market. It also helps you to identify your target audience, who are more likely to buy from you because they are interested in products similar to yours.\n\nEg: If you sell jewelry, your niche might be “women between 20 and 30 who like to shop online.” If you sell diet supplements, your niche might be “men who want to lose weight but hate exercise.”It is important for every business owner that knows about his competitors as well so that he can compete with them effectively and win over them by providing better quality services or products at cheaper prices or faster delivery times etc.\n\n2.  Understanding your Customers\n\nUnderstanding your customers is important in any business, but it’s especially crucial if you’re selling products and services online. Ecommerce businesses are highly dependent on their ability to attract and retain customers, so knowing what makes them tick is key. How can you do this? Here are some of the best ways:\n\nUnderstand their demographics: Demographics are simply the characteristics of a population, such as age, gender, income level, and education level. Knowing more about who’s buying from you can help guide decisions about things like pricing (if female millennials love your products but middle-aged men don’t buy them), product design (if older women aren’t into digital devices), marketing campaigns (if millennials love referral programs) or even hiring practices (if most employees are under 30)\nYou may also want to look at how these demographics have been behaving lately—for example: Are they moving into larger homes? Do they prefer organic foods over processed ones? The answers could help determine which markets will be most profitable for your business model going forward!\nUnderstand their behavior patterns: across different channels – When someone visits an eCommerce website there’s a good chance they’re looking for something specific like clothing sizes or shoe sizes that match their body type so we make sure all our inventory has those options available because otherwise, we would lose out on sales opportunities.\nThis means focusing on improving customer service through both front-end user experience improvements such as better search functionality or back-end order processing improvements such as faster shipping speeds in order to maximize customer satisfaction levels in both cases since happier customers tend to spend more money over time.\n\n3. What Kind of Product do you Sell?\n\nMany eCommerce companies recommend using this idea. You need to understand the product you want to sell. You need to understand the market you are selling to. You should also know your competition, who they are, what they do and how they work. What is their pricing like?\n\nYou should research thoroughly the supply chain and distribution of your products.\n\nResearching thoroughly will help you in understanding how things move along in the supply chain and where exactly your product will come from when it reaches its destination, whether that’s a warehouse or a customer’s house.\n\nLast but not least, don’t forget about marketing! Marketing is important for any business whether online or offline because without marketing no one knows about your business so make sure that you have good advertising strategies in place before starting out with eCommerce ventures.\n\n4. Have a Plan B\n\nHaving a Plan B is important because, while you want your business to succeed, it is not going to be the only thing you do in life. You are going to have other things going on that might take your attention away from the business.One more reason why having a backup plan is important: sometimes things don’t go according to plan! It’s often possible for entrepreneurs who have done their research and planned carefully still face problems along their way.Unexpected expenses can arise, customers may react differently than expected, government policies may change, competitors might enter the market unexpectedly… You name it! The list goes on forever! This is why having contingency plans ready beforehand will help prevent major losses while making sure there’s always something left over if something goes wrong with one part of our strategy. Many web design company in Bangalore have used this shortcut to success in previous years.\n\n5. Be Aware of the Competitors\n\nWhile you are determining the feasibility of your eCommerce business, it’s important that you also take a look at your competitors. If there are no competitors in the industry, then this is not a good sign for an eCommerce business.\n\nYou should do some research on them and understand their strengths and weaknesses. Know more about their price points, marketing strategies, and customer service.\n\nConclusion\n\nWe hope these tips have given you some insight into the world of e-commerce and how to make it work for you. It’s important to remember that e-commerce is not a one-size-fits-all solution for your business needs.\n\nEvery business owner has different goals and priorities, so take the time to evaluate what those are before committing yourself or your company to any particular course of action. know about these before starting your ecommerce store.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Overview\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You may have heard people saying ‘Do what you love and the money will follow’ or ‘Build your passion and then pursue it full-time’. While these phrases may be true for some, today’s reality is that entrepreneurship can come with many challenges.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>One of them is financial security. Creating a new business is a risky endeavor and there are no guarantees that it will be successful. But if you plan in advance before starting your eCommerce business you can minimize the risk. An E-commerce web design agency’s suggests the top 5 things to consider before starting an eCommerce business:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/5-things-to-consider-before-starting-an-ecommerce-business\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">5 Things to Consider Before Starting an Ecommerce Business</a></strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"5 Things You Need to Know Before Starting an eCommerce Business\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Knowing your Niche\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A niche is a small group of people with a shared interest in something specific. The more focused your niche, the better you can serve them and the more money you will make. Many <a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/ecommerce-web-development-india/bangalore/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">E-commerce website development companies</a> recommend this point. Knowing your niche is the first step toward starting an eCommerce business.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you want to start your own eCommerce business, you need to know about the product, market, and competitors in detail. Knowing your niche helps you to focus on a particular segment of the market. It also helps you to identify your target audience, who are more likely to buy from you because they are interested in products similar to yours.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Eg: If you sell jewelry, your niche might be “women between 20 and 30 who like to shop online.” If you sell diet supplements, your niche might be “men who want to lose weight but hate exercise.”It is important for every business owner that knows about his competitors as well so that he can compete with them effectively and win over them by providing better quality services or products at cheaper prices or faster delivery times etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2.  Understanding your Customers\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Understanding your customers is important in any business, but it’s especially crucial if you’re selling products and services online. Ecommerce businesses are highly dependent on their ability to attract and retain customers, so knowing what makes them tick is key. How can you do this? Here are some of the best ways:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":true,\"items\":[\"<strong>Understand their demographics:</strong> Demographics are simply the characteristics of a population, such as age, gender, income level, and education level. Knowing more about who’s buying from you can help guide decisions about things like pricing (if female millennials love your products but middle-aged men don’t buy them), product design (if older women aren’t into digital devices), marketing campaigns (if millennials love referral programs) or even hiring practices (if most employees are under 30)\",\"You may also want to look at how these demographics have been behaving lately—for example: Are they moving into larger homes? Do they prefer organic foods over processed ones? The answers could help determine which markets will be most profitable for your business model going forward!\",\"<strong>Understand their behavior patterns:</strong> across different channels – When someone visits an eCommerce website there’s a good chance they’re looking for something specific like clothing sizes or shoe sizes that match their body type so we make sure all our inventory has those options available because otherwise, we would lose out on sales opportunities.<br>This means focusing on improving customer service through both front-end user experience improvements such as better search functionality or back-end order processing improvements such as faster shipping speeds in order to maximize customer satisfaction levels in both cases since happier customers tend to spend more money over time.\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. What Kind of Product do you Sell?\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Many eCommerce companies recommend using this idea. You need to understand the product you want to sell. You need to understand the market you are selling to. You should also know your competition, who they are, what they do and how they work. What is their pricing like?</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You should research thoroughly the supply chain and distribution of your products.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Researching thoroughly will help you in understanding how things move along in the supply chain and where exactly your product will come from when it reaches its destination, whether that’s a warehouse or a customer’s house.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Last but not least, don’t forget about marketing! Marketing is important for any business whether online or offline because without marketing no one knows about your business so make sure that you have good advertising strategies in place before starting out with eCommerce ventures.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Have a Plan B\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Having a Plan B is important because, while you want your business to succeed, it is not going to be the only thing you do in life. You are going to have other things going on that might take your attention away from the business.One more reason why having a backup plan is important: sometimes things don’t go according to plan! It’s often possible for entrepreneurs who have done their research and planned carefully still face problems along their way.Unexpected expenses can arise, customers may react differently than expected, government policies may change, competitors might enter the market unexpectedly… You name it! The list goes on forever! This is why having contingency plans ready beforehand will help prevent major losses while making sure there’s always something left over if something goes wrong with one part of our strategy. <a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">Many web design company in Bangalore</a> have used this shortcut to success in previous years.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Be Aware of the Competitors\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>While you are determining the feasibility of your eCommerce business, it’s important that you also take a look at your competitors. If there are no competitors in the industry, then this is not a good sign for an eCommerce business.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You should do some research on them and understand their strengths and weaknesses. Know more about their price points, marketing strategies, and customer service.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>We hope these tips have given you some insight into the world of e-commerce and how to make it work for you. It’s important to remember that e-commerce is not a one-size-fits-all solution for your business needs.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Every business owner has different goals and priorities, so take the time to evaluate what those are before committing yourself or your company to any particular course of action. know about these before starting your ecommerce store.</p>\"}]}]}]}', '5 Things to Consider Before Starting an Ecommerce Business', 'Before starting any kind of ecommerce startups you should consider some of those. here we have listed 5 Things to Consider Before Starting an Ecommerce Business.', '/uploads/blog/202410-c918878f60133cc9.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'e-commerce'), 'published', '2024-10-16 07:03:09', '2024-10-16 07:03:09', '2026-07-16 10:40:50');
INSERT IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, blocks, meta_title, meta_description, cover, category_id, status, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('how-to-build-an-ecommerce-website-complete-guide', 'How to Build an Ecommerce website-Complete Guide', 'Popularly known as eCommerce in a short form, electronic commerce involves buying and selling products online. It redefined the way businesses function. Besides, it also allows businesses to make tra…', 'Introduction\n\nPopularly known as eCommerce in a short form, electronic commerce involves buying and selling products online. It redefined the way businesses function. Besides, it also allows businesses to make transactions more accessible.\n\nWith a myriad of activities right from marketplaces to retail stores and digital services,  eCommerce brings the possibility for businesses to increase their reach among customers.\n\nAnd for this, they don’t need to follow any geographical barrier. So, if you are seeking to develop an online store for your business, you should go through this eCommerce website development guide.\n\nIt lets businesses connect with their customers 24/7 and prompts them to purchase products and services based on their comfort and time. It doesn’t require businesses to have a physical store of products they sell.\n\nIn today’s digital era, eCommerce witnessed immense growth for various reasons, be it secure payment gateways, advancement in technology, or improved logistics.\n\nIt brings vast growth opportunities to every business irrespective of their size and ensures their future growth. Before delving into how to develop eCommerce website, let’s understand some other related information.\n\nRelated Links:\n\n5 Things to Consider Before Starting an Ecommerce Business\n\nHow to Build eCommerce Website Development? Step By Step Process\n\nBelow mentioned complete guide for ecommerce website development is helpful to understand the basics while development.\n\n1. Website name and domain is the priority\n\nChoosing a website name also will be called as the URL name shouldn’t be taken lightly because it can help your audience relate to your business. It is recommended that you choose a name that is somehow related to your business, or a name that tells your audience what you sell just by reading the website name.After you have decided on the name of your website, the next is to purchase a domain name. You can go for domain registrar services like GoDaddy, Bluehost, Google Domains, etc. As you enter your business or website name on the registrar of your choice, the domain will let you know whether your desired name is available or not.Don’t be upset if you find that your domain name is not available, because your registrar will recommend alternate names. Like, you don’t want another recommendation, you can use other domain names like .net, .co, instead of .com.\n\nShopify — Easy to Use: Easy to use; Customization: Limited to Shopify apps and themes; Scalability: Small and mid-sized business; Hosting: Offers hosting for stores; Cost: Monthly subscription with transaction fees; SEO: Highly secured; Security: Availability of SEO plugins and features\nMagento — Easy to Use: Need technical expertise to use; Customization: Fully customizable and good for large and complex stores; Scalability: Good for large organizations for its scalability; Hosting: Needs a separate hosting for your website; Cost: Higher cost for hosting and development; SEO: Highly secured; Security: Good SEO capabilities\nWooComm-erce — Easy to Use: Need technical expertise to create and customize; Customization: Fully customizable with different themes and plugins; Scalability: Needs a separate hosting for an eCommerce store; Hosting: Free with paid hosting, themes, extensions; Cost: Needs a separate hosting for an eCommerce store; SEO: Highly secured; Security: Powerful SEO features\nHubspot — Easy to Use: User friendly; Customization: Limited customization compared to other platforms; Scalability: Scalable for both small and mid-sized businesses; Hosting: Needs a separate hosting for an online store; Cost: Higher cost for hosting and development; SEO: Highly secure; Security: The latest SEO features are available\n\n2. Choose an eCommerce platform\n\nChoosing an eCommerce platform decides a lot of aspects of your website because this is where your website lives and takes up space. There are many eCommerce platforms where you can find various features that make it easier for building eCommerce websites, and some are free platforms. WordPress is one of the most popular eCommerce platforms used for free eCommerce websites.You can also go for dedicated eCommerce or go for free platforms based on your convenience.\n\n3. Dedicated eCommerce platforms\n\nWant a full-fledged eCommerce ready within a short time? Your best bet is a dedicated eCommerce platform. The dedicated platforms provide expandability, along with fast development solutions. It offers various built-in functionality that speeds up the process of website development, like, secure payments, shipping labels, marketing and various other sales support.\n\nDedicated platforms charge somewhere around $30 per month.\n\n4. Free eCommerce website platforms\n\nFree ecommerce platforms bring eCommerce functionalities but with limitations. They let you sell products or services for free, there is a limit to how many products you can list. Free platforms also have only limited functionalities or features for building stores. Platforms like Ecwid offer up to 10 products for a free listing, but you can also use this platform for listing more items by upgrading to the paid version. Another platform called Free web store provides up to 20 free listings of products.\n\n5. Websites with eCommerce functionalities\n\nWix and Weebly are two of the popular websites that offer various eCommerce functionalities. If you have a website on one of these sites for promoting your brand, and you are recently considering adding eCommerce functionalities, then you can simply switch to the eCommerce plan.\n\n6. It’s now time for building the website\n\nWhat will your eCommerce website consist of? As a website owner, you will have to work with a team or individuals to add value to your website. Some of the elements that your website needs are:\n\n7. A logo or visuals on the website\n\nEvery business or a brand needs a logo – to which the audience can connect your business. You can either hire a designer for creating the logo for your brand, or use the same logo if you already have one. Other than that, you can also check out Canva for creating a free logo yourself.\n\n8. Product photos, descriptions, and data\n\nProduct photos, descriptions and related data are some of the most important parts of developing an eCommerce website. One of the limitations of online shopping is that a potential buyer cannot hold the product in hand, feel the material or can tell its measurement by just seeing a random picture. For that, you must provide multiple pictures of the same product, accurate details and other related data to ensure that your potential buyer knows everything before they buy.\n\n9. Your Story\n\nDon’t write a random story, or keep it all generic in the About Us section. Or worse, don’t avoid keeping one. You have an eCommerce website and have a chance to tell a story to your audience, no matter how small or common it is.\n\n10. Customer service pages\n\nCustomer service can be unique to different businesses, and as an eCommerce business owner, you need to provide services that keep your customer happy. Some of the common service that makes you a wholesome business are:\n\n11. Mentioning shipping rates and timelines\n\nPotential customers like to evaluate both -the timings of when the product will reach them and the price that will be added to the MRP of the product for shipping. Stating the same will help with transparency.\n\n12. Returns and exchanges\n\nIt is common for customers to face situations where they want to return or exchange an order. Clearly state whether you offer returns or exchanges, and if yes, who will pay for those shipping charges.\n\n13. Blog content\n\nBlog contents are often considered indirect marketing and are quite effective albeit taking longer than direct marketing. You can update your website’s blog at a given frequency to increase the rank of your website on the SERPs. Blogs can be shared on your social media profiles also to get better visibility.\n\n14. Set up payment, tax, shipping, and marketing tools\n\nSetting up payment, tax, shipping, etc., is often made easier by eCommerce functionalities. Platforms like Shopify offer full-fledged eCommerce functionalities that have built-in tax calculations, payment processing, shipping labels, and even various advertising tools.\n\n15. Payment processing and tax table setup\n\nWith plug-and-play integration along with popular payment services like Stripe or PayPal, all eCommerce website platforms are feature-rich in terms of payment processing. Some platforms have their own payment solution, like Shopify, which has Shopify Payments. All you have to do is connect your account to the payment processing and you will be connected.\n\nStripe — Pricing: 2.9% per transaction +$0.30 for online transaction; Quality: Developer-friendly API, good support, and documentation; Integration: Offers a range of APIs and plugins\nRazorpay — Pricing: 2% per transaction +0.25 transaction fee; Quality: Quality services for India-based businesses; Integration: Integration for multiple eCommerce platforms\nInstamojo — Pricing: 5% + 3 transaction fee; Quality: Lack of quality and support compared to other platforms; Integration: Simple API for developers\nPayPal — Pricing: Varies by regions; Quality: Global payment processor with a strong reputation; Integration: Wide range of integration and plugins for different platforms\nAuthorize.Net — Pricing: $ 25 monthly gateway + Per transaction 2.9% + 30¢; Quality: Stable and secure and good for businesses with complex payment needs.; Integration: Offers various APIs, plugins, SDKs, etc., and ensures smooth integration with multiple platforms\nSquare — Pricing: 2.9% + 30¢; Quality: Good for small businesses; Integration: N/A\n\n16. Shipping setup\n\nIntegrating shipping software with your eCommerce platform makes it easier to speed up your order fulfilment. From shipping methods to shipping labels, this functionality makes everything easier.\n\n17. Test before the launch of eCommerce website\n\nAs you reach the last stage of your eCommerce development, tests before launching are very important to all kinds of websites. Although not every website goes through the same kind of tests.\n\necommerce companies allow test ordering features where you can test the whole process of ordering but doesn’t charge you in the payment process. This testing process will eventually help you find bugs if any, and assure you that your site is ready for launch.\n\nAfter launching, it’s all about marketing your brand and listing your business in Google My Business to speed up the process of getting online sales. Many social media ads and Google Adwords ads can help your eCommerce website get the visibility it requires.\n\n5 Benefits of eCommerce Websites\n\nIf you wish to sell your products online, having an eCommerce website is necessary and our guide helps you know how to open an eCommerce store. eCommerce facilitates your customers to buy products and make payments online smoothly. Apart from this, an eCommerce website makes you entitled to avail of several other advantages.\n\n1. Remove Geographical Boundaries\n\nRunning a physical store lets you serve customers from limited areas. An eCommerce website removes geographical boundaries and helps you focus more on target customers even from across the world. Thus, it gives you an excellent chance to increase sales and earn vast revenue.It prompts customers to purchase your products by using mobile apps. An eCommerce website helps sellers decrease friction points and makes it simple for buyers to purchase products from anywhere and anytime. eCommerce website lets customers buy products from the comfort of their homes and also encourages businesses to manage their business operations easily and conveniently.\n\n2. Minimize Operational Cost\n\nA physical store owner often needs to spend on various things, be it in-store staff, rent, inventory management, rental, electricity, etc. These expenses adversely impact the revenue of your business. An eCommerce website helps you get rid of all these expenses.\n\nYou can avail of the liberty to run your business even with a small team with a limited number of staff. You also get an option to use Dropshipping options to remove the necessity of physical products. Saving these costs helps you increase the revenue of your business.\n\n3. Scalable and Flexible\n\nAnother advantage of an eCommerce website is its higher scalability, which enables businesses to flourish even without facing constraints related to any physical stores. An eCommerce store can cater to your changing business needs, Whether you are a startup or a highly established market player.\n\nBe it adding the latest features, product expansions, or improved traffic, it accommodates multiple things. Apart from this, the flexibility of an eCommerce website helps businesses try their fate in the new market. Apart from this, it also lets them try some latest promotional strategies even without minimum investment and risk.\n\n4. Easy to Access for Customers\n\nAs mentioned above, an eCommerce website is easily accessible to people based on their convenience. Whether they seek to browse, compare, or purchase products, they have the liberty to do everything even from the comfort of their home. They can avail of this kind of convenience 24/7 and can shop anytime and from any location based on their availability and leisure time.\n\nApart from this, eCommerce platforms facilitate customers to browse products with search and filters. It makes it easy for customers to find their desired products conveniently. Besides, a responsive design of an eCommerce website ensures its smooth accessibility on multiple devices.\n\n5. Gather Data and Get Customer Insights\n\nWith an eCommerce website,  you can gather data related to your customers. The data helps you to gain a full of customer insights into their preferences, customer behavior, purchasing patterns, etc.\n\nYou can use this kind of information to develop the most effective marketing campaign. Besides, it also helps you personalize the shopping experience of customers, which also makes a significant impact in increasing sales and revenue.\n\nKey Components of a Successful Ecommerce Website\n\nDo you know 90% of eCommerce websites fail? And thus fails to match the expectations of business owners. You can, meanwhile, improve the chance of success of your eCommerce website by considering various crucial factors. Our eCommerce website development guide covers some of these factors.\n\n1. Easy Navigation\n\nEasy navigation is one of the vital factors that determine the success of any eCommerce website. If you are planning to start your own ecommerce website, you must be aware of its importance as well. It ensures customers can easily find products and their related details quickly. Easy navigation ensures your website has a good menu structure, categorized product pages, fully accessible search functionality, etc. Customers can easily spot the right product with the use of logical categories, labels, filters, etc.\n\n2. Mobile Optimization\n\nIf you don’t optimize your eCommerce website for mobile, it will not serve its actual purpose. Responsive design of an eCommerce site can easily adapt to the orientations and screen sizes of your e-commerce store. It ensures a seamless experience. Apart from this, mobile optimization also ensures easy-to-tap buttons, quick loading speed, and more.\n\n3. Intuitive Checkout\n\nA lengthy checkout process often discourages customers from completing the entire process and buying products. It also causes a huge cart abandonment rate. As a result, it leads to a loss of sales. So, all you need to do is implement an intuitive checkout process. It should include multiple features such as progress indicators, guest checkout options, save cart items for the future, etc.\n\n4. Customer Support\n\nExpeditious customer support contributes a lot to making your eCommerce store stand apart from the competition. Make sure your online store provides various options for customer support, including email, live chat, phone, etc. You should also mention an FAQ section to help customers find answers to some of their common queries. It prevents them from getting in touch with your staff quite often.\n\n5. Shipping and Return Information\n\nIt’s vital to make a transparent process for shipping and return policies to create trust among customers. All you need to do is display the shipping cost exactly, available options, and delivery times. Apart from this, you should also provide clear details about your return policy, including the entire return procedure. It boosts the confidence of your customers and encourages them to purchase your products.\n\n6. Secure Payment Gateways\n\nSecurity is something that excels in your brand as a reliable brand thus increasing trust among your customers. You should never leave any stone unturned to make your eCommerce store secure. Using a secure payment gateway reflects that payment-related information regarding customers is fully protected.\n\nSo, you should always use a secured and reputed payment gateway including Stripe, PayPal, Square, etc. to build trust among customers.\n\n7. Inventory management\n\nEffective inventory management is quite necessary for making your eCommerce successful. It’s vital to maintain the accuracy related to the product availability information. It automates the entire process of product restocking, updates the availability of products and displays them accordingly in real-time.\n\n8. Calls to action\n\nA bold and strong call to action encourages customers to take quick action and buy their favorite products. All you need to do is to use the right call to action at the right place. Make sure the CTAs you place are visually appealing and placed with a proper strategy throughout your website. It guides customers throughout their shopping journey.\n\nMain Factors to Take Care in Ecommerce Website Development\n\nAn eCommerce website development is a process that includes multiple steps. Our quick guide of eCommerce website development includes all crucial steps.\n\n1. Choosing the Right eCommerce Platform\n\nLets compare some of the renowned eCommerce platforms and select the best one based on your needs.\n\n2. Factors Influencing Platform Choice\n\nSelecting a perfect eCommerce platform is something business owners often get puzzled with. Our eCommerce website development guide includes certain key factors that you can consider while selecting the right platform to develop your online store.\n\n1. Business Goals\n\nAs one of the crucial things, business goals are something you need to take into account while choosing the perfect eCommerce platform for your business. Your selected platform should support your business objective. Whether you have long-term or short-term objectives, make sure your business supports both.\n\n2. Scalability\n\nEveryone seeks to expand their business horizon in the coming times. So, make sure your selected eCommerce development platform allows you to do the same. The platform should be capable of accommodating increased traffic, transactions, additional product listings, etc.\n\n3. User Experience\n\nUser experience has a pivotal role in making eCommerce business successful. Always select a user-friendly eCommerce platform that should be capable of offering an intuitive shopping experience to customers and thus can make a significant impact on your conversion rate. Your selected platform includes all those features to improve customer journey, including quick loading time, mobile users, easy navigation, etc.\n\n4. Search Engine Optimization\n\nYour online store should have impeccable visibility in search engines to gain more potential customers to increase product sales. Your selected platform should be able to support SEO and provide advanced marketing tools to help you promote your products most effectively.\n\n5. Security\n\nA robust security of your eCommerce website is necessary to prevent hackers. And you can’t make your online store unless you choose a secure platform, which ensures great protection for both your business and customers.\n\n6. Budget\n\nBudget is another crucial factor that you should never forget to consider while selecting the eCommerce platform. You can understand some platforms are free and open-source whereas others are available with a license fee. Of course, budget is crucial but you should never make a selection solely on your budget.\n\n7. Support and Documentary\n\nAdequate support is something that remains of great importance be it for resolving any issue, optimizing, or updating the store. You should always look for the level of support those platforms offer. Regular software updates are crucial.\n\nDesign Your E-commerce Site for More Conversions\n\nThe design of any website is crucial to increase its conversion rate and an eCommerce website is not an exception. Our eCommerce website design complete guide suggests you keep in mind the following points while designing your online store to boost its conversion rate.\n\n1. User-Centric\n\nUser-centric design contributes a lot when it comes to increasing the conversion rate of your website. Make sure you have a website that is easy to navigate and has an intuitive design. It should have a clean layout, search functionality, a user-friendly menu, etc. These are essential to make the user journey amazing.\n\n2. Easy Checkout\n\nA complex checkout adversely impacts the conversion rate of your website. To tackle it, your checkout should ensure a smooth buying journey for customers. Guest checkout is the right option that lets people shop even without account creation. You can also show a progress bar to let your customers know how much journey they have completed and also what to complete.\n\n3. Bold CTAs\n\nAs mentioned, CTAs increase the conversion rate of an eCommerce website. Therefore, make sure your design has proper and bold CTAs. Your CTAs should be able to encourage your customers to take action. You need to implement robust strategies when it comes to CTA placement.\n\n4. Quality Descriptions and Images\n\nYour website should be visually enticing, which is much necessary to increase its conversion rate. You should use high-quality images to showcase your products in a better way and also from different angles. You can also include various options including Zoom-in and Zoom-out and videos if possible.\n\n5. Use Social Proof\n\nAs already mentioned above, building trust is essential to ensure the success rate of any eCommerce website by increasing the conversion rate. You can use customer reviews, social badges, guarantees, etc. to make your website trustworthy. You should ensure proper visibility of these elements. These should be easily accessible to customers.\n\n6. A/B Testing\n\nA/B testing is pivotal to find out ranges of design elements like buttons, product elements, colors, and more. You should go through the user’s feedback regularly. It provides you a chance to find out those areas that should be improved and thus helps you make decisions on the basis of data.\n\neCommerce SEO Best Practices\n\nSearch engine optimization (SEO) is quite necessary to magnify the visibility of your website in search engines. It helps you increase organic traffic to your website and thus boost sales and ROI. Let’s explore some of the practices you can implement to get the best outcomes.\n\n1. A Proper Keyword Research and Optimization Strategy\n\nYou should first chalk out a proper keyword research strategy to find the right keywords for your eCommerce website. You should find out phrases your customers use while purchasing products related to yours. Once you find the right keywords, you can implement these everywhere be it descriptions, titles, meta tags, etc. Using long-tail keywords is always the right choice.\n\n2. Write Eye Catchy Product Descriptions\n\nYou need to always write superior quality, informative, and user-engaging product descriptions. These descriptions are helpful for customers to make an informed decision. It also helps in ranking your online store in search engines. It’s advisable to avoid using plagiarized content.\n\n3. Speed Optimization\n\nYour website loads need to load without taking too much time to improve user experience. It’s vital to enhance search engine optimization. Slow page loading causes a higher bounce rate and thus impacts adversely on search engine rankings. You can also boost your website speed by minimizing unnecessary scripts, using content delivery networks (CDN), and images of websites.\n\n4. Responsive Design\n\nGoogle already made it clear it will prioritize a mobile-friendly design of an eCommerce website when it comes to improving search engine ranking. Therefore, you should always ensure your website is fully optimized for mobile to enhance SEO.\n\n5. Use Schema Markup\n\nSchema markup search has its actual purpose of providing required details to search engines about the products you sell to your customers. It improves product listings in search results, which makes it more informative and appealing to customers.\n\n6. Use Reviews and Ratings\n\nReviews and ratings provide search engines with fresh and the most valuable content, apart from letting potential customers know about the experience of those who already purchased the same. It also helps in building more trust and reliability.\n\nThe 5 Key eCommerce Metrics You Should Be Tracking\n\nThe success of any eCommerce business depends on your ability to utilize real-time data and chalk out your business strategies accordingly. For this, you need to keep an eye on some important metrics which are as follows.\n\n1. Cart Abandonment Rate\n\nThe cart abandonment rate reflects the number of users who don’t complete the entire process of purchase even after adding products to the shopping cart. You need to determine why users fail to complete the checkout process. It helps you build an effective strategy to minimize cart abandon rate, including simplifying the checkout process, retargeting campaigns, incentives, and more.\n\n2. Conversion Rate\n\nWith conversion rate metrics, you can gather information regarding the number of users who take the final action to buy products. When it comes to a higher conversion rate, it reflects your website and product pages are effective and thus convincing visitors to purchase. Analyzing these metrics helps you find out some key areas to improve.\n\n3. Customer Retention Rate\n\nYour business strategy should also focus on retaining past customers. A customer retention rate indicates the number of customers who contribute to purchasing products over time.\n\nIf you have a higher customer retention rate for your business, it reflects your loyal customer base. You can adopt strategies like exceptional customer service, personalized marketing, etc. to improve customer retention.\n\n4. Average Order Value\n\nIt signifies the average amount customers spend on every order. Increasing AOV can certainly have a great impact on the revenue you earn. You can boost your average order value through upselling and cross-selling related products, using loyalty programs, or providing quantity discounts.\n\n5. Cost of Customer Acquisition\n\nWhen it comes to customer acquisition, it determines the overall money you spend on acquiring a new customer for your business. By using this metric, you can easily determine the overall efficiency of your marketing efforts and also the overall budget you spend on it.\n\nCreating a Privacy Policy for eCommerce Stores\n\nCreating a privacy policy is necessary for your online store. It safeguards the personal details of your customers and also creates trust and compliance with legal regulations.\n\nLet’s go through some steps to create a privacy policy for your eCommerce website.\n\nYou can mention clearly what kind of personal details you collect from customers\nMention what’s your purpose of collecting data\nLet your customers know about your strategies to protect their personal information\nMake it clear to your customers whether you share data with 3rd party\nBe clear about your cookie policy\nMention customers’ rights, including corrections, access, and deletion of data\n\nPrivacy policy is vital for various reasons, which are as follows.\n\n1. Adhere Legal Compliance\n\nOne of the primary reasons for having a privacy policy for your eCommerce store is to adhere to the rules and regulations of data protection.\n\n2. Transparency\n\nA privacy policy reflects your effort to maintain transparency in data-handling practices\n\n3. Create Trust\n\nIf you handle your customers’ data responsibly, it builds trust among your customers.\n\n4. Minimize Risk\n\nAnother advantage of privacy policy is it minimizes the risk of legal consequences and penalties caused by data mishandling.\n\n5. Boost Customer’s Confidence\n\nA well-defined privacy policy is also helpful in increasing trust and confidence among your customers.\n\n6. Enhance Brand Reputation\n\nA privacy policy is a reflection of your commitment to customers to ensure the safety of their personal information and thus improves your reputation.\n\nFuture Trends in eCommerce\n\neCommerce is set to witness many more trends in the future as an ever-evolving industry. Some of the trends that our comprehensive guide for ecommerce website development includes are as follows.\n\n1. Voice Commerce\n\nThe emergence of Google Assistant and Amazon’s Alexa brought voice assistants as the most popular thing, which have nowadays become the most common things in our lives. And it prompts eCommerce businesses to adopt this.\n\nThey optimize their online store for voice search to let customers explore fun with voice-based shopping. It enables customers to use their voice commands only to buy products.\n\n2. Augmented Reality\n\nAugmented Reality (AR) has made a great impact on the way people shop online. With the technology, shoppers can avail of the liberty to try clothing virtually and can decide whether it’s the best fit for them or not.\n\nApart from the clothes, shoppers can also place furniture items in their homes virtually or also can test various makeup products. So, it improves the online shopping experience of customers by letting them experience a more interactive and immersive feel.\n\n3. Artificial Intelligence\n\nArtificial Intelligence increased the popularity of personalized shopping experiences as an emerging trend. Machine Learning (ML) has the immense capability to analyze data based on customers’ purchasing history. It recommends customers to buy the best products accordingly. It boosts both customer loyalty and conversion rate.\n\n4. Ethical Shopping\n\nCustomers nowadays are also concerned about the social and environmental impact when shopping. They expect eCommerce business owners to offer sustainable products with the perfect package that should not harm the ecosystem in any way. Those service providers focus on this to experience a more competitive edge.\n\n5. Mobile Shopping\n\nAs we already mentioned, the growing number of Smartphone users brought the trend of mobile shopping into the limelight. It prompts many eCommerce businesses to concentrate on mobile optimization and also develop user-friendly applications that redefine the shopping process with features like easy payment options and one-click purchases.\n\nConclusion\n\nYou are supposed to now have crucial information regarding how an eCommerce store is developed, after going through the above eCommerce website development complete guide. The guide envisages complete details of various steps to plan for developing an eCommerce website. To create your online store, you need to get in touch with a trusted service provider.', '{\"v\":1,\"rows\":[{\"cols\":[{\"widgets\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Introduction\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Popularly known as eCommerce in a short form, electronic commerce involves buying and selling products online. It redefined the way businesses function. Besides, it also allows businesses to make transactions more accessible.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>With a myriad of activities right from marketplaces to retail stores and digital services,  eCommerce brings the possibility for businesses to increase their reach among customers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>And for this, they don’t need to follow any geographical barrier. So, if you are seeking to develop an online store for your business, you should go through this eCommerce website development guide.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It lets businesses connect with their customers 24/7 and prompts them to purchase products and services based on their comfort and time. It doesn’t require businesses to have a physical store of products they sell.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>In today’s digital era, eCommerce witnessed immense growth for various reasons, be it secure payment gateways, advancement in technology, or improved logistics.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It brings vast growth opportunities to every business irrespective of their size and ensures their future growth. Before delving into how to develop eCommerce website, let’s understand some other related information.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"<strong>Related Links:</strong>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p><strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sunsys.in/5-things-to-consider-before-starting-an-ecommerce-business\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">5 Things to Consider Before Starting an Ecommerce Business</a></strong></p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"How to Build eCommerce Website Development? Step By Step Process\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Below mentioned complete guide for ecommerce website development is helpful to understand the basics while development.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Website name and domain is the priority\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Choosing a website name also will be called as the URL name shouldn’t be taken lightly because it can help your audience relate to your business. It is recommended that you choose a name that is somehow related to your business, or a name that tells your audience what you sell just by reading the website name.After you have decided on the name of your website, the next is to purchase a domain name. You can go for domain registrar services like GoDaddy, Bluehost, Google Domains, etc. As you enter your business or website name on the registrar of your choice, the domain will let you know whether your desired name is available or not.Don’t be upset if you find that your domain name is not available, because your registrar will recommend alternate names. Like, you don’t want another recommendation, you can use other domain names like .net, .co, instead of .com.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"<strong>Shopify</strong> — Easy to Use: Easy to use; Customization: Limited to Shopify apps and themes; Scalability: Small and mid-sized business; Hosting: Offers hosting for stores; Cost: Monthly subscription with transaction fees; SEO: Highly secured; Security: Availability of SEO plugins and features\",\"<strong>Magento</strong> — Easy to Use: Need technical expertise to use; Customization: Fully customizable and good for large and complex stores; Scalability: Good for large organizations for its scalability; Hosting: Needs a separate hosting for your website; Cost: Higher cost for hosting and development; SEO: Highly secured; Security: Good SEO capabilities\",\"<strong>WooComm-erce</strong> — Easy to Use: Need technical expertise to create and customize; Customization: Fully customizable with different themes and plugins; Scalability: Needs a separate hosting for an eCommerce store; Hosting: Free with paid hosting, themes, extensions; Cost: Needs a separate hosting for an eCommerce store; SEO: Highly secured; Security: Powerful SEO features\",\"<strong>Hubspot</strong> — Easy to Use: User friendly; Customization: Limited customization compared to other platforms; Scalability: Scalable for both small and mid-sized businesses; Hosting: Needs a separate hosting for an online store; Cost: Higher cost for hosting and development; SEO: Highly secure; Security: The latest SEO features are available\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Choose an eCommerce platform\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Choosing an eCommerce platform decides a lot of aspects of your website because this is where your website lives and takes up space. There are many eCommerce platforms where you can find various features that make it easier for building eCommerce websites, and some are free platforms. WordPress is one of the most popular eCommerce platforms used for free eCommerce websites.You can also go for dedicated eCommerce or go for free platforms based on your convenience.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Dedicated eCommerce platforms\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Want a full-fledged eCommerce ready within a short time? Your best bet is a dedicated eCommerce platform. The dedicated platforms provide expandability, along with fast development solutions. It offers various built-in functionality that speeds up the process of website development, like, secure payments, shipping labels, marketing and various other sales support.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Dedicated platforms charge somewhere around $30 per month.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Free eCommerce website platforms\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Free ecommerce platforms bring eCommerce functionalities but with limitations. They let you sell products or services for free, there is a limit to how many products you can list. Free platforms also have only limited functionalities or features for building stores. Platforms like Ecwid offer up to 10 products for a free listing, but you can also use this platform for listing more items by upgrading to the paid version. Another platform called Free web store provides up to 20 free listings of products.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Websites with eCommerce functionalities\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Wix and Weebly are two of the popular websites that offer various eCommerce functionalities. If you have a website on one of these sites for promoting your brand, and you are recently considering adding eCommerce functionalities, then you can simply switch to the eCommerce plan.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. It’s now time for building the website\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>What will your eCommerce website consist of? As a website owner, you will have to work with a team or individuals to add value to your website. Some of the elements that your website needs are:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"7. A logo or visuals on the website\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Every business or a brand needs a logo – to which the audience can connect your business. You can either hire a designer for creating the logo for your brand, or use the same logo if you already have one. Other than that, you can also check out Canva for creating a free logo yourself.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"8. Product photos, descriptions, and data\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Product photos, descriptions and related data are some of the most important parts of developing an eCommerce website. One of the limitations of online shopping is that a potential buyer cannot hold the product in hand, feel the material or can tell its measurement by just seeing a random picture. For that, you must provide multiple pictures of the same product, accurate details and other related data to ensure that your potential buyer knows everything before they buy.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"9. Your Story\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Don’t write a random story, or keep it all generic in the About Us section. Or worse, don’t avoid keeping one. You have an eCommerce website and have a chance to tell a story to your audience, no matter how small or common it is.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"10. Customer service pages\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Customer service can be unique to different businesses, and as an eCommerce business owner, you need to provide services that keep your customer happy. Some of the common service that makes you a wholesome business are:</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"11. Mentioning shipping rates and timelines\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Potential customers like to evaluate both -the timings of when the product will reach them and the price that will be added to the MRP of the product for shipping. Stating the same will help with transparency.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"12. Returns and exchanges\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It is common for customers to face situations where they want to return or exchange an order. Clearly state whether you offer returns or exchanges, and if yes, who will pay for those shipping charges.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"13. Blog content\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Blog contents are often considered indirect marketing and are quite effective albeit taking longer than direct marketing. You can update your website’s blog at a given frequency to increase the rank of your website on the SERPs. Blogs can be shared on your social media profiles also to get better visibility.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"14. Set up payment, tax, shipping, and marketing tools\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Setting up payment, tax, shipping, etc., is often made easier by eCommerce functionalities. Platforms like Shopify offer full-fledged eCommerce functionalities that have built-in tax calculations, payment processing, shipping labels, and even various advertising tools.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"15. Payment processing and tax table setup\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>With plug-and-play integration along with popular payment services like Stripe or PayPal, all eCommerce website platforms are feature-rich in terms of payment processing. Some platforms have their own payment solution, like Shopify, which has Shopify Payments. All you have to do is connect your account to the payment processing and you will be connected.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":false,\"items\":[\"<strong>Stripe</strong> — Pricing: 2.9% per transaction +$0.30 for online transaction; Quality: Developer-friendly API, good support, and documentation; Integration: Offers a range of APIs and plugins\",\"<strong>Razorpay</strong> — Pricing: 2% per transaction +0.25 transaction fee; Quality: Quality services for India-based businesses; Integration: Integration for multiple eCommerce platforms\",\"<strong>Instamojo</strong> — Pricing: 5% + 3 transaction fee; Quality: Lack of quality and support compared to other platforms; Integration: Simple API for developers\",\"<strong>PayPal</strong> — Pricing: Varies by regions; Quality: Global payment processor with a strong reputation; Integration: Wide range of integration and plugins for different platforms\",\"<strong>Authorize.Net</strong> — Pricing: $ 25 monthly gateway + Per transaction 2.9% + 30¢; Quality: Stable and secure and good for businesses with complex payment needs.; Integration: Offers various APIs, plugins, SDKs, etc., and ensures smooth integration with multiple platforms\",\"<strong>Square</strong> — Pricing: 2.9% + 30¢; Quality: Good for small businesses; Integration: N/A\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"16. Shipping setup\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Integrating shipping software with your eCommerce platform makes it easier to speed up your order fulfilment. From shipping methods to shipping labels, this functionality makes everything easier.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"17. Test before the launch of eCommerce website\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As you reach the last stage of your eCommerce development, tests before launching are very important to all kinds of websites. Although not every website goes through the same kind of tests.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>ecommerce companies allow test ordering features where you can test the whole process of ordering but doesn’t charge you in the payment process. This testing process will eventually help you find bugs if any, and assure you that your site is ready for launch.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>After launching, it’s all about marketing your brand and listing your business in Google My Business to speed up the process of getting online sales. Many social media ads and Google Adwords ads can help your eCommerce website get the visibility it requires.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"5 Benefits of eCommerce Websites\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you wish to sell your products online, having an eCommerce website is necessary and our guide helps you know how to open an eCommerce store. eCommerce facilitates your customers to buy products and make payments online smoothly. Apart from this, an eCommerce website makes you entitled to avail of several other advantages.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Remove Geographical Boundaries\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Running a physical store lets you serve customers from limited areas. An eCommerce website removes geographical boundaries and helps you focus more on target customers even from across the world. Thus, it gives you an excellent chance to increase sales and earn vast revenue.It prompts customers to purchase your products by using mobile apps. An eCommerce website helps sellers decrease friction points and makes it simple for buyers to purchase products from anywhere and anytime. eCommerce website lets customers buy products from the comfort of their homes and also encourages businesses to manage their business operations easily and conveniently.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Minimize Operational Cost\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A physical store owner often needs to spend on various things, be it in-store staff, rent, inventory management, rental, electricity, etc. These expenses adversely impact the revenue of your business. An eCommerce website helps you get rid of all these expenses.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can avail of the liberty to run your business even with a small team with a limited number of staff. You also get an option to use Dropshipping options to remove the necessity of physical products. Saving these costs helps you increase the revenue of your business.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Scalable and Flexible\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Another advantage of an eCommerce website is its higher scalability, which enables businesses to flourish even without facing constraints related to any physical stores. An eCommerce store can cater to your changing business needs, Whether you are a startup or a highly established market player.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Be it adding the latest features, product expansions, or improved traffic, it accommodates multiple things. Apart from this, the flexibility of an eCommerce website helps businesses try their fate in the new market. Apart from this, it also lets them try some latest promotional strategies even without minimum investment and risk.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Easy to Access for Customers\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As mentioned above, an eCommerce website is easily accessible to people based on their convenience. Whether they seek to browse, compare, or purchase products, they have the liberty to do everything even from the comfort of their home. They can avail of this kind of convenience 24/7 and can shop anytime and from any location based on their availability and leisure time.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Apart from this, eCommerce platforms facilitate customers to browse products with search and filters. It makes it easy for customers to find their desired products conveniently. Besides, a responsive design of an eCommerce website ensures its smooth accessibility on multiple devices.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Gather Data and Get Customer Insights\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>With an eCommerce website,  you can gather data related to your customers. The data helps you to gain a full of customer insights into their preferences, customer behavior, purchasing patterns, etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You can use this kind of information to develop the most effective marketing campaign. Besides, it also helps you personalize the shopping experience of customers, which also makes a significant impact in increasing sales and revenue.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Key Components of a Successful Ecommerce Website\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Do you know 90% of eCommerce websites fail? And thus fails to match the expectations of business owners. You can, meanwhile, improve the chance of success of your eCommerce website by considering various crucial factors. Our eCommerce website development guide covers some of these factors.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Easy Navigation\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Easy navigation is one of the vital factors that determine the success of any eCommerce website. If you are planning to start your own ecommerce website, you must be aware of its importance as well. It ensures customers can easily find products and their related details quickly. Easy navigation ensures your website has a good menu structure, categorized product pages, fully accessible search functionality, etc. Customers can easily spot the right product with the use of logical categories, labels, filters, etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Mobile Optimization\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you don’t optimize your eCommerce website for mobile, it will not serve its actual purpose. Responsive design of an eCommerce site can easily adapt to the orientations and screen sizes of your e-commerce store. It ensures a seamless experience. Apart from this, mobile optimization also ensures easy-to-tap buttons, quick loading speed, and more.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Intuitive Checkout\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A lengthy checkout process often discourages customers from completing the entire process and buying products. It also causes a huge cart abandonment rate. As a result, it leads to a loss of sales. So, all you need to do is implement an intuitive checkout process. It should include multiple features such as progress indicators, guest checkout options, save cart items for the future, etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Customer Support\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Expeditious customer support contributes a lot to making your eCommerce store stand apart from the competition. Make sure your online store provides various options for customer support, including email, live chat, phone, etc. You should also mention an FAQ section to help customers find answers to some of their common queries. It prevents them from getting in touch with your staff quite often.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Shipping and Return Information\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It’s vital to make a transparent process for shipping and return policies to create trust among customers. All you need to do is display the shipping cost exactly, available options, and delivery times. Apart from this, you should also provide clear details about your return policy, including the entire return procedure. It boosts the confidence of your customers and encourages them to purchase your products.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Secure Payment Gateways\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Security is something that excels in your brand as a reliable brand thus increasing trust among your customers. You should never leave any stone unturned to make your eCommerce store secure. Using a secure payment gateway reflects that payment-related information regarding customers is fully protected.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>So, you should always use a secured and reputed payment gateway including Stripe, PayPal, Square, etc. to build trust among customers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"7. Inventory management\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Effective inventory management is quite necessary for making your eCommerce successful. It’s vital to maintain the accuracy related to the product availability information. It automates the entire process of product restocking, updates the availability of products and displays them accordingly in real-time.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"8. Calls to action\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A bold and strong call to action encourages customers to take quick action and buy their favorite products. All you need to do is to use the right call to action at the right place. Make sure the CTAs you place are visually appealing and placed with a proper strategy throughout your website. It guides customers throughout their shopping journey.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Main Factors to Take Care in Ecommerce Website Development\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>An eCommerce website development is a process that includes multiple steps. Our quick guide of eCommerce website development includes all crucial steps.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Choosing the Right eCommerce Platform\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Lets compare some of the renowned eCommerce platforms and select the best one based on your needs.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Factors Influencing Platform Choice\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Selecting a perfect eCommerce platform is something business owners often get puzzled with. Our eCommerce website development guide includes certain key factors that you can consider while selecting the right platform to develop your online store.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Business Goals\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As one of the crucial things, business goals are something you need to take into account while choosing the perfect eCommerce platform for your business. Your selected platform should support your business objective. Whether you have long-term or short-term objectives, make sure your business supports both.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Scalability\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Everyone seeks to expand their business horizon in the coming times. So, make sure your selected eCommerce development platform allows you to do the same. The platform should be capable of accommodating increased traffic, transactions, additional product listings, etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. User Experience\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>User experience has a pivotal role in making eCommerce business successful. Always select a user-friendly eCommerce platform that should be capable of offering an intuitive shopping experience to customers and thus can make a significant impact on your conversion rate. Your selected platform includes all those features to improve customer journey, including quick loading time, mobile users, easy navigation, etc.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Search Engine Optimization\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Your online store should have impeccable visibility in search engines to gain more potential customers to increase product sales. Your selected platform should be able to support SEO and provide advanced marketing tools to help you promote your products most effectively.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Security\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A robust security of your eCommerce website is necessary to prevent hackers. And you can’t make your online store unless you choose a secure platform, which ensures great protection for both your business and customers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Budget\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Budget is another crucial factor that you should never forget to consider while selecting the eCommerce platform. You can understand some platforms are free and open-source whereas others are available with a license fee. Of course, budget is crucial but you should never make a selection solely on your budget.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"7. Support and Documentary\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Adequate support is something that remains of great importance be it for resolving any issue, optimizing, or updating the store. You should always look for the level of support those platforms offer. Regular software updates are crucial.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Design Your E-commerce Site for More Conversions\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The design of any website is crucial to increase its conversion rate and an eCommerce website is not an exception. Our eCommerce website design complete guide suggests you keep in mind the following points while designing your online store to boost its conversion rate.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. User-Centric\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>User-centric design contributes a lot when it comes to increasing the conversion rate of your website. Make sure you have a website that is easy to navigate and has an intuitive design. It should have a clean layout, search functionality, a user-friendly menu, etc. These are essential to make the user journey amazing.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Easy Checkout\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A complex checkout adversely impacts the conversion rate of your website. To tackle it, your checkout should ensure a smooth buying journey for customers. Guest checkout is the right option that lets people shop even without account creation. You can also show a progress bar to let your customers know how much journey they have completed and also what to complete.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Bold CTAs\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As mentioned, CTAs increase the conversion rate of an eCommerce website. Therefore, make sure your design has proper and bold CTAs. Your CTAs should be able to encourage your customers to take action. You need to implement robust strategies when it comes to CTA placement.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Quality Descriptions and Images\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Your website should be visually enticing, which is much necessary to increase its conversion rate. You should use high-quality images to showcase your products in a better way and also from different angles. You can also include various options including Zoom-in and Zoom-out and videos if possible.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Use Social Proof\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As already mentioned above, building trust is essential to ensure the success rate of any eCommerce website by increasing the conversion rate. You can use customer reviews, social badges, guarantees, etc. to make your website trustworthy. You should ensure proper visibility of these elements. These should be easily accessible to customers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. A/B Testing\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A/B testing is pivotal to find out ranges of design elements like buttons, product elements, colors, and more. You should go through the user’s feedback regularly. It provides you a chance to find out those areas that should be improved and thus helps you make decisions on the basis of data.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"eCommerce SEO Best Practices\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Search engine optimization (SEO) is quite necessary to magnify the visibility of your website in search engines. It helps you increase organic traffic to your website and thus boost sales and ROI. Let’s explore some of the practices you can implement to get the best outcomes.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. A Proper Keyword Research and Optimization Strategy\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You should first chalk out a proper keyword research strategy to find the right keywords for your eCommerce website. You should find out phrases your customers use while purchasing products related to yours. Once you find the right keywords, you can implement these everywhere be it descriptions, titles, meta tags, etc. Using long-tail keywords is always the right choice.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Write Eye Catchy Product Descriptions\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You need to always write superior quality, informative, and user-engaging product descriptions. These descriptions are helpful for customers to make an informed decision. It also helps in ranking your online store in search engines. It’s advisable to avoid using plagiarized content.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Speed Optimization\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Your website loads need to load without taking too much time to improve user experience. It’s vital to enhance search engine optimization. Slow page loading causes a higher bounce rate and thus impacts adversely on search engine rankings. You can also boost your website speed by minimizing unnecessary scripts, using content delivery networks (CDN), and images of websites.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Responsive Design\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Google already made it clear it will prioritize a mobile-friendly design of an eCommerce website when it comes to improving search engine ranking. Therefore, you should always ensure your website is fully optimized for mobile to enhance SEO.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Use Schema Markup\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Schema markup search has its actual purpose of providing required details to search engines about the products you sell to your customers. It improves product listings in search results, which makes it more informative and appealing to customers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Use Reviews and Ratings\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Reviews and ratings provide search engines with fresh and the most valuable content, apart from letting potential customers know about the experience of those who already purchased the same. It also helps in building more trust and reliability.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"The 5 Key eCommerce Metrics You Should Be Tracking\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The success of any eCommerce business depends on your ability to utilize real-time data and chalk out your business strategies accordingly. For this, you need to keep an eye on some important metrics which are as follows.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Cart Abandonment Rate\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The cart abandonment rate reflects the number of users who don’t complete the entire process of purchase even after adding products to the shopping cart. You need to determine why users fail to complete the checkout process. It helps you build an effective strategy to minimize cart abandon rate, including simplifying the checkout process, retargeting campaigns, incentives, and more.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Conversion Rate\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>With conversion rate metrics, you can gather information regarding the number of users who take the final action to buy products. When it comes to a higher conversion rate, it reflects your website and product pages are effective and thus convincing visitors to purchase. Analyzing these metrics helps you find out some key areas to improve.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Customer Retention Rate\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Your business strategy should also focus on retaining past customers. A customer retention rate indicates the number of customers who contribute to purchasing products over time.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you have a higher customer retention rate for your business, it reflects your loyal customer base. You can adopt strategies like exceptional customer service, personalized marketing, etc. to improve customer retention.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Average Order Value\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>It signifies the average amount customers spend on every order. Increasing AOV can certainly have a great impact on the revenue you earn. You can boost your average order value through upselling and cross-selling related products, using loyalty programs, or providing quantity discounts.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Cost of Customer Acquisition\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>When it comes to customer acquisition, it determines the overall money you spend on acquiring a new customer for your business. By using this metric, you can easily determine the overall efficiency of your marketing efforts and also the overall budget you spend on it.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Creating a Privacy Policy for eCommerce Stores\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Creating a privacy policy is necessary for your online store. It safeguards the personal details of your customers and also creates trust and compliance with legal regulations.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Let’s go through some steps to create a privacy policy for your eCommerce website.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":true,\"items\":[\"You can mention clearly what kind of personal details you collect from customers\",\"Mention what’s your purpose of collecting data\",\"Let your customers know about your strategies to protect their personal information\",\"Make it clear to your customers whether you share data with 3rd party\",\"Be clear about your cookie policy\",\"Mention customers’ rights, including corrections, access, and deletion of data\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Privacy policy is vital for various reasons, which are as follows.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Adhere Legal Compliance\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>One of the primary reasons for having a privacy policy for your eCommerce store is to adhere to the rules and regulations of data protection.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Transparency\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A privacy policy reflects your effort to maintain transparency in data-handling practices</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Create Trust\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>If you handle your customers’ data responsibly, it builds trust among your customers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Minimize Risk\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Another advantage of privacy policy is it minimizes the risk of legal consequences and penalties caused by data mishandling.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Boost Customer’s Confidence\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A well-defined privacy policy is also helpful in increasing trust and confidence among your customers.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"6. Enhance Brand Reputation\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>A privacy policy is a reflection of your commitment to customers to ensure the safety of their personal information and thus improves your reputation.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Future Trends in eCommerce\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>eCommerce is set to witness many more trends in the future as an ever-evolving industry. Some of the trends that our comprehensive guide for ecommerce website development includes are as follows.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"1. Voice Commerce\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>The emergence of Google Assistant and Amazon’s Alexa brought voice assistants as the most popular thing, which have nowadays become the most common things in our lives. And it prompts eCommerce businesses to adopt this.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>They optimize their online store for voice search to let customers explore fun with voice-based shopping. It enables customers to use their voice commands only to buy products.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"2. Augmented Reality\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Augmented Reality (AR) has made a great impact on the way people shop online. With the technology, shoppers can avail of the liberty to try clothing virtually and can decide whether it’s the best fit for them or not.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Apart from the clothes, shoppers can also place furniture items in their homes virtually or also can test various makeup products. So, it improves the online shopping experience of customers by letting them experience a more interactive and immersive feel.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"3. Artificial Intelligence\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Artificial Intelligence increased the popularity of personalized shopping experiences as an emerging trend. Machine Learning (ML) has the immense capability to analyze data based on customers’ purchasing history. It recommends customers to buy the best products accordingly. It boosts both customer loyalty and conversion rate.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"4. Ethical Shopping\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>Customers nowadays are also concerned about the social and environmental impact when shopping. They expect eCommerce business owners to offer sustainable products with the perfect package that should not harm the ecosystem in any way. Those service providers focus on this to experience a more competitive edge.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"html\":\"5. Mobile Shopping\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>As we already mentioned, the growing number of Smartphone users brought the trend of mobile shopping into the limelight. It prompts many eCommerce businesses to concentrate on mobile optimization and also develop user-friendly applications that redefine the shopping process with features like easy payment options and one-click purchases.</p>\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"html\":\"Conclusion\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"html\":\"<p>You are supposed to now have crucial information regarding how an eCommerce store is developed, after going through the above eCommerce website development complete guide. The guide envisages complete details of various steps to plan for developing an eCommerce website. To create your online store, you need to get in touch with a trusted service provider.</p>\"}]}]}]}', 'How to Build an Ecommerce website / online store', 'We are sensing the adoptability for digital world is emerging. If you are a business owner then you must aware of How to Build an Ecommerce website or online store. Here is the complete guide', '/uploads/blog/202410-411d177ab79f4524.webp', (SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug = 'e-commerce'), 'published', '2024-10-16 07:05:14', '2024-10-16 07:05:14', '2025-02-28 06:48:13');
